X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 59": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2383717-a-poetun-poeta-additional-films-and-guests"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_59
SUMMARY:A Poet/Un poeta | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART:20260926T200000Z
DTEND:20260926T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260817T160610Z
UID:20260926T200000Z-2384047@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260926T200000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/81/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1920,1080/32017_A_Poet_1920x1080.rev.1786977917.jpg
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Middle-aged and erratic\, Oscar is a failed writer who has giv
 en up on life. Unemployed and living with family\, he wanders the streets 
 of Medellín in a drunken stupor\, lamenting the state of literature in hi
 s home country\, where he has succumbed to the cliché of the tortured art
 ist. However\, the opportunity to mentor a young student offers a chance a
 t redemption\, if he doesn't screw it up first. In a performance marked by
  darkly comic pathos\, first-time actor Ubeimar Rios stars in Simón Mesa 
 Soto's Un Certain Regard Jury Prize-winner A Poet\, a raw and riotous farc
 e about how good deeds are often met with the universe's idea of cruel and
  unusually poetic punishment. [123 min\; comedy\, drama\; Spanish with Eng
 lish subtitles]
GEO:39.168613;-86.517376
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T200610Z
LOCATION:IU CINEMA
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2383717-a-poetun-poeta-additional-fi
 lms-and-guests
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Middle-aged and erratic\, Oscar is a fai
 led writer who has given up on life. Unemployed and living with family\, h
 e wanders the streets of Medellín in a drunken stupor\, lamenting the sta
 te of literature in his home country\, where he has succumbed to the clich
 é of the tortured artist. However\, the opportunity to mentor a young stu
 dent offers a chance at redemption\, if he doesn't screw it up first. In a
  performance marked by darkly comic pathos\, first-time actor Ubeimar Rios
  stars in Simón Mesa Soto's Un Certain Regard Jury Prize-winner <i>A Poet
 </i>\, a raw and riotous farce about how good deeds are often met with the
  universe's idea of cruel and unusually poetic punishment. [123 min\; come
 dy\, drama\; Spanish with English subtitles]</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <a href="mailto:iucinema@iu.edu">iucinema@
 iu.edu</a> // 812-856-CINE\n</p>
