ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/251/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/118,0,781,663/32438_IMG_5344a_jpg.rev.1788981135.png
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Functions, festivals, and celebrations,He
 alth and wellness,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:The Tree School Presents… Listening to and With Trees: A Ful
 l Moon Deep Listening and Sound Gathering with Composer and Harpist Gabrie
 l Jenks  We welcome you to the first in our series of being with trees at 
 night.  Step away from the noise and tune into the nocturnal rhythm of the
  180-year-old Bur Oak.&#160\;  Beneath its majestic canopy\, we will begin
  the evening with a series of guided deep listening practices\, opening ou
 r awareness to each other and the teaching presence of the tree.  As we se
 ttle in and the full moon begins to rise\, award-winning Jacobs School of 
 Music composer and musician Gabriel Jenks (https://music.indiana.edu/facul
 ty/current_adjunct/jenks-gabriel.html) will improvise on the harp a real-t
 ime soundscape in collaboration with the moon\, the tree\, the night\, and
  all of us together.  Come dream\, imagine\, listen\, and restore.What to 
 Bring  A favorite blanket\, yoga mat\, or chair to listen comfortably on t
 he ground. Bring an open heart\, big ears\, and a desire to rest deeply wi
 th the wisdom of the Bur Oak at night.Rain Policy  In the event of incleme
 nt weather\, this event will be rescheduled. Registered guests will receiv
 e an update via email at 4:00 PM on the day of the event. Registration is 
 not required\, though much appreciated.&#160\;Contact  Any questions? Reac
 h out to Catherine Bowman (cabowman@iu.edu (mailto:cabowman@iu.edu)) or Ka
 ylie Fougerousse (kefouger@iu.edu (mailto:kefouger@iu.edu)).&#160\;Funded 
 by IU Research through the Public Arts and Humanities Project.&#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T163200Z
LOCATION:The historic Bur Oak tree in front of the IMU\, by Dunn Meadow ju
 st off 7th Street
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2412353-listening-to-and-with-trees-
 a-full-moon-deep
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>The Tree School Presents… Listen
 ing to and With Trees: A Full Moon Deep Listening and Sound Gathering with
  Composer and Harpist Gabriel Jenks</strong></p><p>  We welcome you to the
  first in our series of being with trees at night.</p><p>  Step away from 
 the noise and tune into the nocturnal rhythm of the 180-year-old Bur Oak.&
 #160\;</p><p>  Beneath its majestic canopy\, we will begin the evening wit
 h a series of guided deep listening practices\, opening our awareness to e
 ach other and the teaching presence of the tree.</p><p>  As we settle in a
 nd the full moon begins to rise\, award-winning Jacobs School of Music com
 poser and musician <a href="https://music.indiana.edu/faculty/current_adju
 nct/jenks-gabriel.html">Gabriel Jenks</a> will improvise on the harp a rea
 l-time soundscape in collaboration with the moon\, the tree\, the night\, 
 and all of us together.<br />  Come dream\, imagine\, listen\, and restore
 .</p><p><strong>What to Bring</strong><br />  A favorite blanket\, yoga ma
 t\, or chair to listen comfortably on the ground. Bring an open heart\, bi
 g ears\, and a desire to rest deeply with the wisdom of the Bur Oak at nig
 ht.</p><p><br /><strong>Rain Policy</strong><br />  In the event of inclem
 ent weather\, this event will be rescheduled. Registered guests will recei
 ve an update via email at 4:00 PM on the day of the event. Registration is
  not required\, though much appreciated.&#160\;</p><p><br /><strong>Contac
 t</strong></p><p>  Any questions? Reach out to Catherine Bowman (<a href="
 mailto:cabowman@iu.edu">cabowman@iu.edu</a>) or Kaylie Fougerousse (<a hre
 f="mailto:kefouger@iu.edu">kefouger@iu.edu</a>).&#160\;</p><p><em>Funded b
 y IU Research through the Public Arts and Humanities Project.&#160\;</em><
 /p><p><picture class="lw_image lw_image32512  lw_align_left"><source media
 ="(max-width: 500px)" type="image/webp" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live
