X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Monroe Lake 296 Calendar Ics": "https://events.in.gov/event/activity-center-craft-of-the-day-paynetown-sra-monroe-lake"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_monroe_lake_296_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20260926T045225Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52772841234878
DTSTART:20260927T170000Z
DTEND:20260927T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Paynetown Activity Center (Paynetown SRA\, next to the Swimming
  Beach)\n\nMemorial Day Weekend thru mid-August on THURSDAY-SUNDAY from 1 
 to 5 p.m.Mid-August thru October on SATURDAY-SUNDAY from 1 to 5 p.m.Craft 
 of the Day: Make a different craft each day!\n\nView our live snakes\, che
 ck out the wall exhibits and taxidermy collection\, or consult our referen
 ce library.\n\nThe Naturalist’s Office is located inside the Activity Ce
 nter. You can also pick up maps/brochures/flyers or browse our library of 
 field guides and other books.\n\nNeed to fill a little time (or a rainy af
 ternoon?) Sit down at our puzzle table (500-1500 piece puzzles designed fo
 r older children and adults) or play one of our board games.\n\nJust for k
 ids! The kid’s corner has a puppet stage\, games\, puzzles\, large felt 
 board\, picture books\, touch table\, and a “small world” playscape. T
 here’s also a coloring table and a selection of kid-friendly board games
 .\n\nRecycle your aluminum cans with us! Proceeds fund programs\, activiti
 es\, and exhibits. You can also recycle plastic bottles and paper (no food
  containers).
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Activity Center / Craft of the Day\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/activity-center-craft-of-the-day-
 paynetown-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Monroe Lake 296 Calendar Ics": "https://events.in.gov/event/stillwater-levee-walk-stillwater-northfork-wra-monroe-lake"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_monroe_lake_296_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20260926T045225Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53533623990816
DTSTART:20260927T170000Z
DTEND:20260927T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Stillwater Levee Walk at 1:00 p.m.\n\n•    Sign up at tinyurl
 .com/stillwater2026 by September 25.\n•    Limited to 20 people\, recomm
 ended for adults.\n•    Location: Meet at Northfork Check Station on Ken
 t Road\n\nJoin us for a hike along the levees of Stillwater Marsh to learn
  how Monroe Lake manages this area with wildlife in mind! We’ll explore 
 the crops planted for wildlife food\, check out the nesting boxes\, see wh
 ere (and how) the marsh gets flooded each year to create a seasonal wetlan
 d\, and explore the types of trees\, plants\, and animals that live here. 
 2 hours
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Meet at Northfork Check Station on Kent Road (direct
 ions will be emailed to registrants)
SUMMARY:Stillwater Levee Walk\, Stillwater-Northfork WRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/stillwater-levee-walk-stillwater-
 northfork-wra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
