DESCRIPTION:Spend the night celebrating the Mid-Autumn Festival with tradi
 tional mooncakes and tongyun\, games like mahjong\, and the opportunity t
 o create lanterns out of craft paper. The Mid-Autumn Festival is a tradit
 ional celebration across China\, Hong Kong\, and many other East and Sout
 hEast Asian countries. It's a celebration of thanksgiving for the autumn 
 harvest. Families spend this night enjoying the moon\, eating mooncakes w
 ith egg yolks to represent the moon\, and eating a meal together. The fes
 tival has been around for almost 3000 years.\nAll Indiana University even
 ts\, groups\, activities\, and educational\, cultural\, and historical ob
 servances welcome all IU students and other members of the Indiana Univer
 sity community.\n\nHosted by: Hong Kong Students Association\, Indiana Me
 morial Union Board\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://bei
 nvolved.indiana.edu/event/12781771
