SUMMARY:A Well-Advised Lunch with David Conte
DESCRIPTION:Student Sign Up here &gt\;  A prolific composer across all ge
 nres\, David is the composer of over 150 works published by E. C. Schirme
 r Music Company\, and has received commissions from the San Francisco\, D
 ayton\, Oakland\, and Stockton Symphonies\, the Lee Trio\, the Ives Quart
 et\, Chanticleer\, the American Choral Directors Association Raymond Broc
 k Commission\, the American Guild of Organists\, Sonoma City Opera and th
 e Gerbode Foundation for his opera America Tropical. He has also served o
 n the composition faculty of the San Francisco Conservatory of Music sinc
 e 1985\, becoming department chair in 2015\, and has studied with some of
  the most prominent figures in American music composition\, including Aar
 on Copland and Nadia Boulanger. Don't miss your opportunity to enrich you
 r own career path with advice from David's own fascinating journey!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><a href="https://iubloomington.joinhandsh
 ake.com/events/2026776/share_preview"><strong>Student Sign Up here &gt\;<
 /strong></a></p><p>  A prolific composer across all genres\, David is the
  composer of over 150 works published by E. C. Schirmer Music Company\, a
 nd has received commissions from the San Francisco\, Dayton\, Oakland\, a
 nd Stockton Symphonies\, the Lee Trio\, the Ives Quartet\, Chanticleer\, 
 the American Choral Directors Association Raymond Brock Commission\, the 
 American Guild of Organists\, Sonoma City Opera and the Gerbode Foundatio
 n for his opera America Tropical. He has also served on the composition f
 aculty of the San Francisco Conservatory of Music since 1985\, becoming d
 epartment chair in 2015\, and has studied with some of the most prominent
  figures in American music composition\, including Aaron Copland and Nadi
 a Boulanger. Don't miss your opportunity to enrich your own career path w
 ith advice from David's own fascinating journey!</p>
