X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364527-preparing-for-systematic-reviews-of-the-literature-u"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Preparing for Systematic Reviews of the Literature using the PRISM
 A-Protocols Framework
DTSTART:20260929T190000Z
DTEND:20260929T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T150347Z
UID:20260929T190000Z-2364527@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260929T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1920,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 785270700.jpg
CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:While incredibly powerful\, it requires a significant amount o
 f time and preparation to be done well. Attendees of this webinar will lea
 rn best practices for preparing for Evidence Synthesis (which includes Sys
 tematic Reviews\, Scoping Reviews\, Umbrella Reviews\, etc.)\, and the too
 ls and support available to IU researchers.__________  New to research\, n
 ew to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about resear
 ch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us
  for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching with 
 data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requ
 irements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Res
 earch Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for 
 researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.
   For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Servic
 es team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to che
 ck back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T225210Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2364527-preparing-for-systematic
 -reviews-of-the-literature-u
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">While incredibl
 y powerful\, it requires a significant amount of time and preparation to b
 e done well. Attendees of this webinar will learn best practices for prepa
 ring for Evidence Synthesis (which includes Systematic Reviews\, Scoping R
 eviews\, Umbrella Reviews\, etc.)\, and the tools and support available to
  IU researchers.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:fals
 e\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&quot\;3355
 59739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</span
 ></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested 
 in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of the
  Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through th
 e basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing you
 r data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.</p><p> 
  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus 
 partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some session
 s may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, please co
 ntact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto:resdat
 a@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regularly\,
  as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
