DESCRIPTION:Bring a meaningful keepsake to be digitized and share its stor
 y for the archive at this 3D scanning drop-in session exploring how person
 al objects\, stories\, and emerging tehnologies can shape new forms of par
 ticipatory archiving. Participants may also experience how these collectiv
 e contributions are being transfored into an interactive installation in t
 he KIX Lab.  Megan Young\, senior lecturer of digital art in the Eskenazi 
 School\, and Nicole Miller\, director of 3D fabrication and design inquiry
  labs at the Luddy School\, lead the session.  The event is presented by t
 he IU Kinetic Immersion and Extended Reality Lab (KIX Lab)\, IU Luddy Scho
 ol of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering\, IU Research\, and the Eske
 nazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design.  More information is available
  through Megan Young at young19@iu.edu.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T192532Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2422875-exploring-meaning-and-rec
 ognition-across-immersive
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Bring a meaningful keepsake to be digiti
 zed and share its story for the archive at this 3D scanning drop-in sessio
 n exploring how personal objects\, stories\, and emerging tehnologies can 
 shape new forms of participatory archiving. Participants may also experien
 ce how these collective contributions are being transfored into an interac
 tive installation in the KIX Lab.</p><p>  Megan Young\, senior lecturer of
  digital art in the Eskenazi School\, and Nicole Miller\, director of 3D f
 abrication and design inquiry labs at the Luddy School\, lead the session.
 </p><p>  The event is presented by the IU Kinetic Immersion and Extended R
 eality Lab (<span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">KIX Lab)\, IU Luddy S
 chool of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering\, IU Research\, and the E
 skenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design.</span></p><p>  More informa
 tion is available through Megan Young at young19@iu.edu.</p>
