SUMMARY: Honoring Charlotte Zietlow: A Memorial
DESCRIPTION:Please join us at Switchyard Pavilion on Thursday\, October 1
 \, from 3:00–5:00 PM\, as we celebrate the life and legacy of Charlotte Z
 ietlow (1934–2025).\n\nCharlotte was a pioneering public servant\, commun
 ity advocate\, and catalyst for change in Bloomington and Monroe County.\
 n\nOver a career spanning five decades\, she broke new ground as the firs
 t woman to serve as President of Bloomington City Council\, and later as 
 the first woman to lead the Monroe County Board of Commissioners.\n\nA sc
 holar of German and French literature\, Charlotte brought a global perspe
 ctive to everything she touched from civic leadership to her love of cook
 books and international culture.\n\nShe was also a devoted nonprofit lead
 er\, supporting organizations including Planned Parenthood and Middle Way
  House.\n\nCharlotte left an indelible mark on our community and the many
  lives she touched. We hope you'll join us to honor her life and memory.
CATEGORIES:
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62fb9509b27fd5
 06428328ed/6aaaa46f01f78b0ebd7f9432/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Please join us at Switchyard Pavilion on Thursday\, 
 October 1\, from 3:00–5:00 PM\, as we celebrate the life and legacy of Ch
 arlotte Zietlow (1934–2025)....
LOCATION:Switchyard Pavilion\,1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\,
  USA
