SUMMARY:Open Studio: First Thursdays
DTSTART:20261001T200000Z
DTEND:20261001T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260819T115450Z
UID:20261001T200000Z-2386386@events.iu.edu__20261001
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,640,427/10126_xxeducation_openstudio_09292021_31_o4.rev.1
 639584631.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Health and wellness
DESCRIPTION:Our Open Studio program invites participants to be creative in
  the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for reflection\, expre
 ssion\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist\, the open studi
 o welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their own pace while drawi
 ng inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art experience is need
 ed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, and we'll handle t
 he rest!  Participants are welcome to utilize supplies located in the stud
 io\, as well as bring their own supplies/projects to work on.  This progra
 m occurs during First Thursday each month. It is open to everyone: student
 s\, staff\, and the public included! The group will meet in the Roehm Fami
 ly Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Education on 
 the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T155450Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2386374-open-studio-first-thursdays
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Our Open Studio program invites particip
 ants to be creative in the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool 
 for reflection\, expression\, and connection. Guided by a trained art ther
 apist\, the open studio welcomes visitors to engage with materials at thei
 r own pace while drawing inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No 
 art experience is needed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to creat
 e\, and we'll handle the rest!</p><p>  Participants are welcome to utilize
  supplies located in the studio\, as well as bring their own supplies/proj
 ects to work on.</p><p>  This program occurs during First Thursday each mo
 nth. It is open to everyone: students\, staff\, and the public included! T
 he group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, located inside 
 the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum o
 f Art.</p>
