SUMMARY: October First Thursdays Festival
DESCRIPTION:First Thursdays showcase the diversity of arts and humanities
  at IU Bloomington and offer a welcoming environment for students\, facul
 ty\, staff\, and community members to explore new creative outlets. Each 
 event is a unique opportunity to experience the wonderful work of artists
 \, performers\, and scholars from across campus and around town.\n\nThe O
 ctober First Thursdays will be a festival highlighting the work of arts &
  humanities groups on campus and in the community. The event is free and 
 open to the public and will feature 90+ a&h-focused activity booths\, 35+
  arts & crafts vendors\, performances\, extended gallery hours\, food tru
 cks\, giveaways\, and more. Around the IU Fine Arts Plaza\, there will be
  activities and performances paying tribute to the late Dolly Parton\, a 
 “make your own monster” craft station\, a mobile blood drive\, and animal
  ambassadors\, among many other activities. On the main stage\, we’ll hav
 e performances by Tipa Tipo\, Bloomington Delta Music Club\, IU Musical T
 heatre\, and an interactive Bad Bunny Pilates demonstration!\n\nFirst Thu
 rsdays are hosted by the IU Arts & Humanities Council. For more informati
 on and volunteer opportunities\, please visit go.iu.edu/first-thursdays h
 ttp://go.iu.edu/first-thursdays .
CATEGORIES:Music,Free,In-Person
