DESCRIPTION:This tour starts with a visit to a listening station\, hosted 
 by IU Archives of African American Music and Culture (https://aaamc.indian
 a.edu/)\, where guests can hear Billie Holliday's song Strange Fruit\, whi
 ch is connected with Jones' diptych Poplar Trees. Then\, the tour heads to
  the third floor to explore the new featured exhibition Samuel Levi Jones:
  An Archaeology of Knowledge. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2
 026-09-12-samuel-levi-jones-archaeology-of-knowledge.html)Know Before You 
 GoWalk-ins are welcome if there's space. To reserve a space\, RSVP below.P
 lan to arrive at least 5 minutes before your tour to check in and get read
 y.A small handbag may be carried at your side. Larger bags and backpacks m
 ust be stored before touring. Free lockers are available.Where to find us\
 , where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelinesWhen You ArriveChec
 k in with Guest Services staff on the first floor.Photography is welcome\,
  without flash or selfie stick.Please do not touch artwork.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T112955Z
