CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;Dr. Yoletty Bracho will examine neo-imperialism\, neoco
 lonialism\, and grassroots resistance\, drawing on the Venezuelan case.  B
 racho is a researcher and adjunct professor of political science at the Un
 iversité d'Avignon in southern France and an Impact+ postdoctoral fellow 
 at the Université de Montréal. She holds a PhD in political sociology fr
 om the Université Lumière Lyon 2 and specializes in participatory public
  policy and left-wing activism in Venezuela. She is currently working on h
 er book manuscript\, Faire la Révolution dans l'État : participation et 
 consolidation autoritaire au Venezuela\, with Éditions Terres de feu.
