 /strong></p><p class="intro"><em>Breakfast served at 9am</em></p><p class=
 "intro"><strong>Hamilton Lugar School -</strong><strong>Shreve Auditorium<
 /strong></p><p class="intro"><strong>For Schedule</strong>: <a href="https
 ://crres.indiana.edu/events/venezuela-symposium.html">Center for Research 
 Race &amp\; Ethnicity in Society's Event Page</a>&#160\;</p><p>  Against t
 he backdrop of political upheaval\, foreign intervention\, natural disaste
 r\, and long-standing infrastructure challenges\, <em><strong>Venezuelan P
 olitics in the Wake of Crisis</strong></em> will bring together scholars a
 nd a human rights advocate for an interdisciplinary examination of contemp
 orary Venezuela.</p><p>  The symposium will feature <strong>Verónica Zubi
 llaga</strong> of the University of Illinois Chicago and <strong>Yoletty B
 racho</strong> of Avignon University\, joining in person\; <strong>Magdale
 na López</strong> of the University of Notre Dame and the University Inst
 itute of Lisbon\, joining virtually\; and Venezuelan attorney and human ri
 ghts advocate <strong>Venus Marina Faddoul Barrios</strong>\, director of 
 the NGO 100% Estrógeno\, joining virtually from Spain.</p><p>  Drawing on
  expertise in political participation\, urban and state violence\, cultura
 l criticism\, human rights\, and gender justice\, the panelists will exami
 ne how Venezuela's continuing crises have affected political life\, civil 
 society\, migration and displacement\, and regional relations. The program
  will also include a screening of <em><strong>22 de mayo</strong></em> (19
 69) by <strong>Cine Urgente</strong> moderated by <strong>Dr. Noraeden Mor
 a</strong> from the Department of Spanish and Portuguese.</p><p>  Organize
 d by the Center for Research on Race and Ethnicity in Society (CRRES)\, in
  collaboration with the Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies (C
 LACS)\, the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies (HLS
 )\, the Department of History\, and the Department of Spanish and Portugue
 se.</p>
