ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/363/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1350/32393_IG_Post_Poster.BookParty.3.rev.1788793327
 .png
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Join us in celebrating the recent publication of Sadistic Chol
 as: Transfeminist Provocations in Contemporary Peru (University of Texas P
 ress) by Olga Rodríguez-Ulloa\, Interim Director of the Latino Studies Pr
 ogram and Assistant Professor of English\, American Studies\, and Latino S
 tudies.Sadistic Cholas examines contemporary art and activism in Peru that
  reappropriate the racial slur "chola" as a site of political and aestheti
 c intervention. Through a transfeminist lens\, Rodríguez-Ulloa explores h
 ow racialized women reclaim and transform the term to advance forms of pol
 itical and aesthetic liberation.  Following a discussion of the book and R
 odríguez-Ulloa's scholarship\, we'll celebrate with music and a festive g
 athering. This is a 21+ event.
GEO:39.165184;-86.534423
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T155759Z
LOCATION:The Back Door
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2409558-book-party-sadistic-cholas-b
 y-olga-rodriguez-ulloa
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us in celebrating the recent public
 ation of <em>Sadistic Cholas: Transfeminist Provocations in Contemporary P
 eru</em> (University of Texas Press) by Olga Rodríguez-Ulloa\, Interim Di
 rector of the Latino Studies Program and Assistant Professor of English\, 
 American Studies\, and Latino Studies.</p><p><em>Sadistic Cholas</em> exam
 ines contemporary art and activism in Peru that reappropriate the racial s
 lur "chola" as a site of political and aesthetic intervention. Through a t
 ransfeminist lens\, Rodríguez-Ulloa explores how racialized women reclaim
  and transform the term to advance forms of political and aesthetic libera
 tion.</p><p>  Following a discussion of the book and Rodríguez-Ulloa's sc
 holarship\, we'll celebrate with music and a festive gathering. This is a 
 21+ event.</p>
