DESCRIPTION:Special Documentary Screening • Faculty Panel • ReceptionO
 ctober 3 | 5:00–8:00 PMShreve Auditorium  Global and International Studi
 es Building  355 N. Eagleson Ave.\, BloomingtonHow did Taiwan build a semi
 conductor industry from scratch—and transform it into a global technolog
 ical force?  Directed by Chu-chen Hsiao\, A Chip Odyssey tells the story o
 f Taiwan's semiconductor industry through interviews with more than 80 peo
 ple who witnessed and shaped its development—from pioneering engineers a
 nd female factory workers to policymakers\, technology veterans\, and a ne
 w generation of engineers confronting new challenges.  Join us for a speci
 al screening followed by a multidisciplinary conversation with Indiana Uni
 versity faculty exploring Taiwan's semiconductor industry\, technological 
 innovation\, and its broader global significance.PROGRAM5:00 PM  Welcome R
 emarks5:10 PMA Chip Odyssey Screening6:45 PM  Faculty Panel Discussion fea
 turing:&#160\;Chen-Ting Liao\, Associate Professor\, Department of Physics
 Isak Nti Asare\, Co-Director\, Cybersecurity and Global Policy Program\; A
 ssistant Dean for Undergraduate Education and Student Affairs&#160\;Sagar 
 Samtani\, Associate Professor\, Director of Kelley's Data Science and Arti
 ficial Intelligence LabChung-chieh Shan\, Associate Professor\, Luddy Scho
 ol of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering7:15–8:00 PM  Light Recep
 tionJOIN THE CONVERSATION  Discover the people and history behind Taiwan's
  semiconductor transformation and engage with IU specialists from across d
 isciplines for a deeper conversation about technology\, innovation\, and T
 aiwan's IT sector.Organized by  IU Taiwan Studies Initiative  East Asian S
 tudies Center  Taipei Economic and Cultural Office (TECO) in Chicago
