DESCRIPTION:$100 first-place prize in each category          Top 3 photos 
 in each category will be displayed in GISB Atrium\, Nov 16 - 20.          
 Winning photos will be permanently displayed in the Global and Internation
 al Studies Building.    Who can enter?  Any HLS student who studied abroad
  Fall 2025\, Spring 2026\, Summer 2026 or Academic Year 2025-2026.  Photos
  must have been taken during your study abroad experience in your host cou
 ntry.Photo Submission CategoriesMost Picturesque: Capture a memorable land
 scape\, cityscape\, landmark\, or other scene from your host country    Cu
 ltural Exchange: Share a moment that reflects meaningful engagement with o
 r learning about your host community and culture    A Day in the Life:&#16
 0\;Show us a moment that captures what everyday life was like during your 
 time abroad.    Photos that feature you and your IU spirit are encouraged!
 A few things to know before you submit:  Photos should tell the story of y
 our study abroad experience while respectfully representing the people and
  places you encounteredMake sure people pictured are comfortable being pho
 tographed and having the photo publicly displayed  Photo featuring childre
 n or minors are not permitted  Do not submit photos featuring dangerous/pr
 ohibited activities\, alcohol or drugs.&#160\;  Avoid photos that stereoty
 pe\, exploit\, or disrespect people or cultures  Follow photography rules 
 at religious\, memorial\, governmental\, and culturally significant sites 
  Review the full photo ethics and contest guidelines (https://indiana-my.s
 harepoint.com/:w:/g/personal/ellcohen_iu_edu/IQCuZXL_BuC3SJQbjsVO7gvaAbUpX
 29xqtIFzjJ7JXaPBlY?e=6PUNCr)Photo Specifications  Submit your original\, h
 ighest resolution photo (preferably 900 x 720 megapixels or greater)–not
  a screenshot or imagine downloaded from social media.  Low-resolution ima
