X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2425012-war-paint-women-at-war-art-and-a-movie", "IU Cinema": "https://events.iu.edu/cinemaiub/event/2425012-war-paint-women-at-war-art-and-a-movie", "Pillar Arts Community Calendar": "https://tockify.com/bloomington.arts.calendar/detail/2442/1791133200000"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 234": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2425012-war-paint-women-at-war-art-and-a-movie"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_234
SUMMARY:War Paint: Women at War | Art and a Movie
DTSTART:20261004T170000Z
DTEND:20261004T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T112916Z
UID:20261004T170000Z-2428014@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261004T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/81/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1920,1081/32615_War_Paint_1920x1080.rev.1790003942.jpg
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Margy Kinmonth's feature documentary shines a light on the tra
 ilblazing role of women war artists\, on the frontlines round the world\, 
 championing the female perspective on conflict through art. Culture breaks
  the taboo\, crosses borders—tells the truth to power. Artists discussed
  include: Zhanna Kadyrova\, Linda Kitson\, Shirin Neshat\, Rachel Reckitt\
 , Dame Laura Knight\, Lee Miller\, Nina Berman\, Marcelle Hanselaar\, Jana
 nne Al-Ani\, Assil Diab\, Doris Zinkeisen\, Fiona Banner aka The Vanity Pr
 ess\, Maggi Hambling\, Cornelia Parker\, Dame Rachel Whiteread\, Maya Lin\
 , and including the work of Anne Desmet R.A.\, Samar Hussaini\, and featur
 ing Dame Penelope Lively\, Charlotte Johnstone\, and Ami Bouhassane. A cas
 t of women contributors and crew makes this film a unique undertaking\, te
 lling vital truths in turbulent times. War Paint: Women at War is the thir
 d installment in Kinmonth's trilogy of films about how artists depict war\
 , following the acclaimed Eric Ravilious: Drawn to War and War Art with Ed
 die Redmayne. [89 min\; documentary\, war\; English]This program is presen
 ted in partnership with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After the screening\, 
 continue the conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art with a special pro
 gram led by museum photographer Shanti Knight. Register for this free even
 t here.
GEO:39.168613;-86.517376
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T152916Z
LOCATION:IU CINEMA
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2425012-war-paint-women-at-war-art-a
 nd-a-movie
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Margy Kinmonth's feature documentary shi
 nes a light on the trailblazing role of women war artists\, on the frontli
 nes round the world\, championing the female perspective on conflict throu
 gh art. Culture breaks the taboo\, crosses borders—tells the truth to po
 wer. Artists discussed include: Zhanna Kadyrova\, Linda Kitson\, Shirin Ne
 shat\, Rachel Reckitt\, Dame Laura Knight\, Lee Miller\, Nina Berman\, Mar
 celle Hanselaar\, Jananne Al-Ani\, Assil Diab\, Doris Zinkeisen\, Fiona Ba
 nner aka The Vanity Press\, Maggi Hambling\, Cornelia Parker\, Dame Rachel
  Whiteread\, Maya Lin\, and including the work of Anne Desmet R.A.\, Samar
  Hussaini\, and featuring Dame Penelope Lively\, Charlotte Johnstone\, and
  Ami Bouhassane. A cast of women contributors and crew makes this film a u
 nique undertaking\, telling vital truths in turbulent times. <i>War Paint:
  Women at War</i> is the third installment in Kinmonth's trilogy of films 
 about how artists depict war\, following the acclaimed <i>Eric Ravilious: 
 Drawn to War</i> and <i>War Art</i> with Eddie Redmayne. [89 min\; documen
 tary\, war\; English]</p><p><i><strong>This program is presented in partne
 rship with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After the screening\, continue the 
 conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art with a special program led by m
 useum photographer Shanti Knight. Register for this free event </strong></
 i><a class="external" href="https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2399916-
 art-a-movie-at-the-eskenazi-museum-women"><i><strong>here</strong></i></a>
 <i><strong>.</strong></i></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <a href="mailto:iucinema@iu.edu">iucinema@
 iu.edu</a> // 812-856-CINE\n</p>
