X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2399916-art-a-movie-at-the-eskenazi-museum-women"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Art & a Movie at the Eskenazi Museum: Women Photographers with Sha
 nti Knight
DTSTART:20261004T190000Z
DTEND:20261004T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T141434Z
UID:20261004T190000Z-2403577@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261004T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,26,816,841/32259_Screenshot_2026-08-28_at_11.45.15AM.rev.17
 87931965.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:3:00-3:30 p.m. Martin Commons\, 2nd floor  Knight will present
  a talk exploring the contributions of women photographers throughout hist
 ory. Drawing inspiration from themes raised in War Paint\, the lecture wil
 l highlight the important role women have played behind the camera\, often
  in the face of significant barriers\, as well as women's current challeng
 es and opportunities within the profession.3:30-4:00 p.m. "Ask Me Anything
 " conversation with Knight. She will share insights from her work as the E
 skenazi Museum of Art's photographer and reflect on her experiences as a f
 ull-time professional photographer.  After the program\, guests will recei
 ve a list featuring works by women photographers in the museum's collectio
 n and in The Photographic Reflex. From 4:00-5:00 p.m.\, visitors are invit
 ed to explore the museum independently and spend time with these artworks.
 Bio:Shanti Knight has been the photographer at Eskenazi Museum of Art sinc
 e 2019. She began working in the field as a teenager\, growing up in her f
 ather's photography business and starting her independent practice in her 
 20s. She earned her Bachelor of Arts in Journalism with a Second Concentra
 tion in Fine Arts from Indiana University in 2011. She launched her career
  in New York City with an internship at Glamour magazine. In the years fol
 lowing\, she has assisted\, shot for\, and received direct training and me
 ntorship from more than 30 different professional photographers\, mostly h
 igh-end professionals in New York City and Chicago with a variety of speci
 alties\, including\, but not limited to\, wedding\, editorial\, fashion\, 
 and commercial work\, and she has served clients from coast to coast.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T181434Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2399916-art-a-movie-at-the-eskenazi-
 museum-women
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>3:00-3:
 30 p.m. Martin Commons\, 2nd floor</strong></p><p style="font-weight: 400\
 ;">  Knight will present a talk exploring the contributions of women photo
 graphers throughout history. Drawing inspiration from themes raised in <em
 >War Paint</em>\, the lecture will highlight the important role women have
  played behind the camera\, often in the face of significant barriers\, as
  well as women's current challenges and opportunities within the professio
 n.</p><p><strong>3:30-4:00 p.m.</strong> "Ask Me Anything" conversation wi
 th Knight. She will share insights from her work as the Eskenazi Museum of
  Art's photographer and reflect on her experiences as a full-time professi
 onal photographer.</p><p>  After the program\, guests will receive a list 
 featuring works by women photographers in the museum's collection and in <
 em>The Photographic Reflex</em>. From 4:00-5:00 p.m.\, visitors are invite
 d to explore the museum independently and spend time with these artworks.<
 /p><p><span data-markjs="true">Bio:</span><span data-markjs="true">Shanti<
 /span> Knight has been the photographer at Eskenazi Museum of Art since 20
 19. She began working in the field as a teenager\, growing up in her fathe
 r's photography business and starting her independent practice in her 20s.
  She earned her Bachelor of Arts in Journalism with a Second Concentration
  in Fine Arts from Indiana University in 2011. She launched her career in 
 New York City with an internship at <em>Glamour</em> magazine. In the year
 s following\, she has assisted\, shot for\, and received direct training a
 nd mentorship from more than 30 different professional photographers\, mos
 tly high-end professionals in New York City and Chicago with a variety of 
 specialties\, including\, but not limited to\, wedding\, editorial\, fashi
 on\, and commercial work\, and she has served clients from coast to coast.
 </p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Emily Zarse<br />\n  Public Experiences Ma
 nager<br />\n  eczarse@iu.edu\n</p>
