 diana.edu/careers/dc-global-policy-program/index.html)This session is desi
 gned specifically for students in the Cybersecurity and Global Policy join
 t degree.  Whether your goal is a residency at CISA\, the Department of Ju
 stice\, the NSA\, or a private sector tech policy firm\, this is your chan
 ce to see how the D.C. residency functions as a professional launchpad for
  your technical expertise.What to Expect:The Cyber Pipeline: Guidance on i
 dentifying and securing D.C. internship placements that value the Luddy/HL
 S joint-degree background.    Day One Readiness: How our "tradecraft" mode
 l prepares you to brief officials on complex cyber threats from your first
  day in the capital.    The Roadmap: A technical walkthrough of the Octobe
 r 15 application deadline and the 2027 semester start date for the Spring 
 cohort.    Interested in the Summer Forum instead? Drop on in!        We k
 now your schedule is tight. Drop in for 20 minutes to grab lunch and the "
