 614 BCX2">We'll discuss everything from file organization and naming conve
 ntions to writing documentation that future users will understand.</span><
 /span> We'll</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW28045811 BCX2">cover cho
 osing</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW28045811 BCX2">appropriate file
 </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW28045811 BCX2">formats\, creating a 
 data dictionary or codebook\, and handling common issues like de-identific
 ation and missing data notes. Participants will leave with a checklist the
 y can apply to their own data before</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW
 28045811 BCX2">submitting</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW28045811 BC
 X2">to a repository.</span></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">______
 ____</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or i
 nterested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the cou
 rse of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you 
 through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and s
 toring your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tool
 s.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and oth
 er campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. So
 me sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\,
  please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a class="ex
 ternal" href="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forge
 t to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
