X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/cahi/event/2426870-humanities-hangout-with-rachel-whitney-iu-ba-04-inte"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Humanities Hangout with Rachel Whitney (IU B.A. '04\, Internationa
 l Studies + Spanish)
DTSTART:20261005T200000Z
DTEND:20261005T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260922T152229Z
UID:20261005T200000Z-2426870@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261005T200000Z
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Full description:  Would you like to learn how your major or m
 inor in the humanities gives you important preparation that will help you 
 in many different professional fields?  If so\, please join us for a Human
 ities Hangout on Monday\, October 5\, at 4 pm in Maxwell Hall\, with Rache
 l Whitney (IU B.A. '04\, International Studies + Spanish\; MBA\, Vanderbil
 t University).  Ms. Whitney will speak about how a humanities perspective 
 has influenced her approach to business\, problem solving\, decision makin
 g\, working with others\, and more.  Ms. Whitney has worked in music in Na
 shville for 20 years. She has focused in particular on the intersection of
  music and technology. She has worked at YouTube and Pandora and\, most re
 cently\, has spent five years at Spotify as the Head of Editorial for Nash
 ville\, where she led the team that covers rock and alternative\, country\
 , and Christian and gospel music programming. Before working in music prog
 ramming\, she was Director of Digital Marketing at Borman Entertainment. S
 he currently serves on the board of the Americana Music Association and ha
 s also served on the boards of the Country Music Association and Leadershi
 p Music.  Come see how exploring your interests in the humanities can help
  you prepare for a variety of careers!  Pizza will be served.  This series
  is presented by the College Arts + Humanities Institute and the Departmen
 t of Spanish and Portuguese. If you need assistance\, or if you have quest
 ions about physical access\, please email cahi@iu.edu or call (812) 856-11
 69. Accommodations can be made to meet most needs.
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T192538Z
LOCATION:Gayle Karch Cook Center at Maxwell Hall
URL:https://events.iu.edu/cahi/event/2426870-humanities-hangout-with-rache
 l-whitney-iu-ba-04-inte
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Full description:</strong></p><p> 
  Would you like to learn how your major or minor in the humanities gives y
 ou important preparation that will help you in many different professional
  fields?</p><p>  If so\, please join us for a Humanities Hangout on Monday
 \, October 5\, at 4 pm in Maxwell Hall\, with Rachel Whitney (IU B.A. '04\
 , International Studies + Spanish\; MBA\, Vanderbilt University).</p><p>  
 Ms. Whitney will speak about how a humanities perspective has influenced h
 er approach to business\, problem solving\, decision making\, working with
  others\, and more.</p><p>  Ms. Whitney has worked in music in Nashville f
 or 20 years. She has focused in particular on the intersection of music an
 d technology. She has worked at YouTube and Pandora and\, most recently\, 
 has spent five years at Spotify as the Head of Editorial for Nashville\, w
 here she led the team that covers rock and alternative\, country\, and Chr
 istian and gospel music programming. Before working in music programming\,
  she was Director of Digital Marketing at Borman Entertainment. She curren
 tly serves on the board of the Americana Music Association and has also se
 rved on the boards of the Country Music Association and Leadership Music.<
 /p><p>  Come see how exploring your interests in the humanities can help y
 ou prepare for a variety of careers!</p><p>  Pizza will be served.</p><p> 
  This series is presented by the College Arts + Humanities Institute and t
 he Department of Spanish and Portuguese. If you need assistance\, or if yo
 u have questions about physical access\, please email cahi@iu.edu or call 
 (812) 856-1169. Accommodations can be made to meet most needs.</p>
