BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2418608-fall-2026-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-edua", "IU Jacobs School of Music": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2418608-fall-2026-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-edua"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2418608-fall-2026-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-edua"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium with Eduardo Herrera
DTSTART:20261006T200000Z
DTEND:20261006T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T152456Z
UID:20261006T200000Z-2428209@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261006T200000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/137/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2000,2000/32516_CLACS_Faculty_Research_Logo_WHITE.rev.178
 9485744.jpg
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s,Sporting events
DESCRIPTION:CLACS welcomes Eduardo Herrera (Folklore and Ethnomusicology) 
 for the first CLACS Faculty Research presentation of the Fall 2026 semeste
 r. Join us as he presents:Sounds of the World Cup: Fan Atmospheres\, Colle
 ctive Affect\, and Sonic PracticesAbstract:&#160\;Drawing on ethnographic 
 fieldwork conducted during the 2026 FIFA Men's World Cup in Buenos Aires\,
  this presentation examines how sound\, collective memory\, and national n
 arratives shaped Argentine experiences of the final stages of the tourname
 nt. Focusing on the contrasting atmospheres surrounding Argentina's semifi
 nal against England and final against Spain\, I consider how the historica
 l memory of the Malvinas/Falklands War\, comparisons between Lionel Messi 
 and Diego Maradona\, and newly circulating World Cup chants intensified th
 e affective stakes of watching and supporting the national team. Photograp
 hs\, field recordings\, and video illustrate how collective sounding and e
 mbodied participation transformed World Cup spectatorship into a powerful 
 site for experiencing national belonging\, historical memory\, anticipatio
 n\, and defeat.  &#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T192456Z
LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2418608-fall-2026-clacs-faculty-rese
 arch-symposium-with-edua
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  CLACS welcomes <strong>Eduardo Herrera</
 strong> (Folklore and Ethnomusicology) for the first CLACS Faculty Researc
 h presentation of the Fall 2026 semester. Join us as he presents:<strong><
 br /></strong></p><p><strong><em>Sounds of the World Cup: Fan Atmospheres\
 , Collective Affect\, and Sonic Practices<br /></em></strong></p><p><stron
 g>Abstract:&#160\;</strong></p><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody"
 >Drawing on ethnographic fieldwork conducted during the 2026 FIFA Men's Wo
 rld Cup in Buenos Aires\, this presentation examines how sound\, collectiv
 e memory\, and national narratives shaped Argentine experiences of the fin
 al stages of the tournament. Focusing on the contrasting atmospheres surro
 unding Argentina's semifinal against England and final against Spain\, I c
 onsider how the historical memory of the Malvinas/Falklands War\, comparis
 ons between Lionel Messi and Diego Maradona\, and newly circulating World 
 Cup chants intensified the affective stakes of watching and supporting the
  national team. Photographs\, field recordings\, and video illustrate how 
 collective sounding and embodied participation transformed World Cup spect
 atorship into a powerful site for experiencing national belonging\, histor
 ical memory\, anticipation\, and defeat.</span></p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><pic
 ture class="lw_image lw_image32544  lw_align_left"><source media="(max-wid
 th: 500px)" type="image/webp" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/sca
 le/2x/gid/137/width/500/height/669/32544_clacs_faculty_research_symposium_
 HERRERA.rev.1789575440.webp 2x" data-origin="responsive"/><source media="(
 max-width: 500px)" type="image/jpeg" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/im
 age/scale/2x/gid/137/width/500/height/669/32544_clacs_faculty_research_sym
 posium_HERRERA.rev.1789575440.jpg 2x" data-origin="responsive"/><source me
 dia="(min-width: 501px)" type="image/webp" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/l
 ive/image/gid/137/width/609/height/815/32544_clacs_faculty_research_sympos
 ium_HERRERA.rev.1789575440.webp 1x" data-origin="responsive"/><source medi
 a="(min-width: 501px)" type="image/jpeg" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/liv
 e/image/gid/137/width/609/height/815/32544_clacs_faculty_research_symposiu
 m_HERRERA.rev.1789575440.jpg 1x" data-origin="responsive"/><img width="609
 " height="815" alt="" data-alt="" data-decoration="true" src="https://even
 ts.iu.edu/live/image/gid/137/width/609/height/815/32544_clacs_faculty_rese
 arch_symposium_HERRERA.rev.1789575440.jpg" title="clacs faculty research s
 ymposium - 1" data-max-w="1088" data-max-h="1456" loading="lazy" data-opti
 mized="true"/></picture></p>
