CATEGORIES:Art, music, films, and performances,Community events,Functions,
  festivals, and celebrations
DESCRIPTION:"ExcursionsIntothe Weird\," is an exhibition of paintings by a
 rtist\, author\, and longtime Bradbury friend John CarterTibbetts\, openin
 g October 1 at the Cultural Arts Galleryat IUIndianapolis. Drawing on memo
 ries and influences spanning Tibbetts' life\, the exhibition traces what h
 e describes as a path away from "the commonplace and the ordinary" and tow
 ard the wonderful\, extraordinary\, and terrifying. The exhibition will re
 main on view throughout October.Presented as part of Festival451indy.Festi
 val 451indy is sponsored in part by Herbert Simon Family Foundation with a
 dditional support from Indiana Humanities
GEO:39.774049;-86.175938
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T161658Z
LOCATION:Cultural Arts Gallery
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2388264-excursions-into-the-weird-cu
 ltural-arts-gallery
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span class="TextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8" lan
 g="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTextRun
  SCXW9873833 BCX8">"Excursions</span><span class="NormalTextRun Contextual
 SpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW9873833 BCX8">Into</span><span class="
 NormalTextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8">the Weird\," is an exhibition of paintings
  by artist\, author\, and longtime Bradbury friend <strong>John C</strong>
 </span><strong><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8">arter</span></
 strong><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8"><strong>Tibbetts</stro
 ng>\, opening October 1 at the Cultural Arts Gallery</span><span class="No
 rmalTextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8">at IU</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW9
 873833 BCX8">Indianapolis</span></span><span class="TextRun SCXW9873833 BC
 X8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="Normal
 TextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8">. Drawing on memories and influences spanning Ti
 bbetts' life\, the exhibition traces what he describes as a path away from
  "the commonplace and the ordinary" and toward the wonderful\, extraordina
 ry\, and terrifying. The exhibition will remain on view throughout October
 .</span></span></p><p><span class="TextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8" lang="EN-US" 
 xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW98738
 33 BCX8">Presented as part of Festival451indy.</span></span></p><p><span c
 lass="TextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contras
 t="auto"><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW9873833 BCX8">Festival 451indy is 
 sponsored in part by Herbert Simon Family Foundation with additional suppo
 rt from Indiana Humanities</span></span></p>
