X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Korean Rice Cake Workshop
DTSTART:20261008T150000Z
DTEND:20261008T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T153505Z
UID:20261008T150000Z-2402248@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261008T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/177/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1545,1999/32406_Rice_Cake_Workshop_Flyer.rev.1788880633.p
 ng
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, October 8thAvailable sessions:&#160\;  Session 1: 1
 1:00 - 12:30 p.m.  Session 2: 2:00 - 3:30 p.m. FULL - all new registered p
 articipants will be put on the waitlistAt GISB 1060&#160\;355 N Eagleson A
 v.  Bloomington 47405  &#160\;  This event is free and open to the public.
 &#160\;  All materials will be provided.&#160\;  RSVP ONLY  &#160\;About S
 ongpyeon:  Songpyeon (송편) is a traditional Korean treat made of glutin
 ous rice. It is a type of tteok (떡)\, small rice cakes\, traditionally e
 aten during the Korean autumn harvest festival\, Chuseok (추석). Songpye
 on symbolizes a full moon and was used for ancestral celebrations along wi
 th other foods to show appreciation for the year's harvest. Koreans hoped 
 and prayed to help them avoid misfortune.About&#160\;Jennifer Lee Ban:Jenn
 ifer Lee Ban\, also known as Mama Ban\, is the founder of Rice Blossoms\, 
 a modern Korean dessert brand rooted in tradition and wellness. After beco
 ming a new mom\, she struggled to find wholesome snacks for her daughters 
 while seeking a creative outlet after stepping away from her career as a p
 rofessional interior designer. Her search led her to the art of Korean des
 sert-making\, where she discovered beautifully crafted treats that were bo
 th nourishing and deeply meaningful. Mama Ban was drawn to traditional Kor
 ean rice cakes for their natural qualities—they are gluten-free\, often 
 vegan\, and thoughtfully made. Today\, through Rice Blossoms\, she reimagi
 nes these time-honored desserts with a modern sensibility\, steaming each 
 one with care and intention.&#160\;  You will be able to take your Songpye
 on home!  Light refreshments will be served.&#160\;
GEO:39.170011;-86.517418
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T131950Z
LOCATION:355 North Eagleson Avenue
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2376428-korean-rice-cake-workshop
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Thursday\, October 8th<br /></stro
 ng>Available sessions:&#160\;<br />  Session 1: 11:00 - 12:30 p.m.<br />  
 Session 2: 2:00 - 3:30 p.m. <strong>FULL</strong> - all new registered par
 ticipants will be put on the waitlist</p><p><strong>At GISB 1060&#160\;<br
  /></strong>355 N Eagleson Av.<br />  Bloomington 47405</p><p style="text-
 align: center\;">  &#160\;</p><p style="text-align: center\;">  This event
  is free and open to the public.&#160\;<br />  All materials will be provi
 ded.&#160\;<strong><br /><br />  RSVP ONLY</strong></p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>
 <strong>About Songpyeon:</strong><br />  Songpyeon (송편) is a tradition
 al Korean treat made of glutinous rice. It is a type of tteok ()\, small r
 ice cakes\, traditionally eaten during the Korean autumn harvest festival\
 , Chuseok (추석). Songpyeon symbolizes a full moon and was used for ance
 stral celebrations along with other foods to show appreciation for the yea
 r's harvest. Koreans hoped and prayed to help them avoid misfortune.</p><p
 ><strong>About&#160\;</strong><strong>Jennifer Lee Ban:<br /></strong>Jenn
 ifer Lee Ban\, also known as Mama Ban\, is the founder of Rice Blossoms\, 
 a modern Korean dessert brand rooted in tradition and wellness. After beco
 ming a new mom\, she struggled to find wholesome snacks for her daughters 
 while seeking a creative outlet after stepping away from her career as a p
 rofessional interior designer. Her search led her to the art of Korean des
 sert-making\, where she discovered beautifully crafted treats that were bo
 th nourishing and deeply meaningful. Mama Ban was drawn to traditional Kor
 ean rice cakes for their natural qualities—they are gluten-free\, often 
 vegan\, and thoughtfully made. Today\, through Rice Blossoms\, she reimagi
 nes these time-honored desserts with a modern sensibility\, steaming each 
 one with care and intention.&#160\;</p><p style="text-align: center\;"><br
  />  You will be able to take your Songpyeon home!<br />  Light refreshmen
 ts will be served.&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  iks@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2402248
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/177/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1545\,1999/32406_Rice_Cake_Workshop_Flyer.re
 v.1788880633.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Rice Cake Workshop Flyer
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Come and join our workshop to learn how to make
  the traditional Korean Songpyeon with the founder of Rice Blossoms!&#160\
 ;\n</p>\n<p>\n  Two sessions available:&#160\;\n</p>\n<p>\n  Session 1: 11
 :00 - 12:30 p.m.<br />\n  Session 2: 2:00 - 3:30 p.m. <strong>FULL&#160\;<
 /strong>\n</p>
