BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Eskenazi School of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344744-homeschool-day-cloth-and-culture", "Architecture + Design": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344744-homeschool-day-cloth-and-culture", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2344744-homeschool-day-cloth-and-culture"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344744-homeschool-day-cloth-and-culture"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Cloth and Culture
DTSTART:20261008T170000Z
DTEND:20261008T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121524Z
UID:20261008T170000Z-2352809@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261008T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1081,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.1783430812.png
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by Indonesian fabrics made by women\, students will d
 iscover how cloth can tell stories about culture\, creativity\, and change
  over time. Through printmaking techniques\, we'll experiment with repetit
 ion and design to create our own patterned handkerchiefs. Join us to explo
 re textile traditions and craft a one-of-a-kind piece inspired by global a
 rtistry!  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in gr
 ades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education
  on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off persona
 l items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will in
 spire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio 
 to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strolle
 rs are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\
 , with one adult for every 6 children.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260716T161524Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344744-homeschool-day-cloth-and-cul
 ture
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Inspired by Indonesian fabrics made by w
 omen\, students will discover how cloth can tell stories about culture\, c
 reativity\, and change over time. Through printmaking techniques\, we'll e
 xperiment with repetition and design to create our own patterned handkerch
 iefs. Join us to explore textile traditions and craft a one-of-a-kind piec
 e inspired by global artistry!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed ar
 t educator for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:<
 /strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd fl
 oor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before
  exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our proj
 ect\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our 
 own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are 
 welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18
  or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Madelyn Cage</strong><br />\n  You
 th and Family Art Education Manager<br />\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Muse
 um of Art<br />\n  <a href="mailto:cagem@iu.edu">cagem@iu.edu<br />\n  812
 -855-0607</a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2352809
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1081\,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.178343081
 2.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Homeschool Day graphic
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Learn how artists use patterns\, colors\, and v
 arious processes to create textiles that are both beautiful and meaningful
 .&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:Architecture + Design, Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Eskenazi School of Art
END:VEVENT
