BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2418613-how-to-build-academic-posters"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:How to Build Academic Posters
DTSTART:20261008T193000Z
DTEND:20261008T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260915T113721Z
UID:20261008T193000Z-2418613@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261008T193000Z
CATEGORIES:Student-run
DESCRIPTION:Join the HLS Graduate Peer Mentors for a practical workshop on
  how to create an effective academic research poster. We'll discuss how to
  organize your research\, communicate your main ideas visually\, and desig
 n a poster that works well for conferences\, symposia\, and other academic
  settings.  This workshop is the first in a series of events leading up to
  the Graduate Student Poster Session at the GAP Symposium at HLS on Novemb
 er 7. A follow-up Academic Poster Workshop on October 29 will provide an o
 pportunity to work on your poster and receive feedback before the symposiu
 m.  No finished project or previous poster experience is required. Whether
  you already have research you would like to present or simply want to lea
 rn more about academic poster design\, you are welcome to join us.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T154531Z
LOCATION:GISB
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2418613-how-to-build-academic-posters
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the HLS Graduate Peer Mentors for a
  practical workshop on how to create an effective academic research poster
 . We'll discuss how to organize your research\, communicate your main idea
 s visually\, and design a poster that works well for conferences\, symposi
 a\, and other academic settings.</p><p>  This workshop is the first in a s
 eries of events leading up to the Graduate Student Poster Session at the G
 AP Symposium at HLS on November 7. A follow-up Academic Poster Workshop on
  October 29 will provide an opportunity to work on your poster and receive
  feedback before the symposium.</p><p>  No finished project or previous po
 ster experience is required. Whether you already have research you would l
 ike to present or simply want to learn more about academic poster design\,
  you are welcome to join us.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2418613
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Join the HLS Graduate Peer Mentors for a practi
 cal workshop on how to create an effective academic research poster.\n</p>
