X-SOURCE-URLS:{"The Comedy Attic": "https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/361517", "Limestone Post": "https://www.comedyattic.com/events/132563", "BloomingtonArts.Today": "https://www.comedyattic.com/events/132563"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"The Comedy Attic": "https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/361515"}
X-SOURCE-ID:comedy_attic
SUMMARY:Kyle Kinane's Triumphant Return to Bloomington!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T210000
UID:20261010-kyle-kinane-s-triumphant-return-to-bloom-1900
DESCRIPTION:Kyle Kinane is a comedian from Addison\, Illinois. According t
 o Wikipedia\, he is a notable person from that town. Other notable residen
 ts of Addison have been the boxer Leon Spinks and a woman who wrote poetry
  about Beanie Babies. Raised in such a cultural fondue pot as this\, it wa
 s natural for Kyle to find his way from warehouse work into show business.
  As a comedian\, he has been seen on The Tonight Show\, Netflix’s “The
  Standups\,” and 5 of his own hour-length specials . As an actor\, he’
 s been in the Judd Apatow series “Love” and truTV’s “Those Who Can
 ’t.” He was also on “Drunk History\,” where he unfortunately wasn
 ’t acting. As a voice over actor\, he was the former voice of Comedy Cen
 tral for 8 years and currently plays Bullet on the Netflix series “Parad
 ise PD.” He is also co-host of the No Accounting for Taste podcast along
  with Shane Torres. As a musician\, he has done nothing\, as he is not a m
 usician. Kyle’s most recent standup work\, “Dirt Nap\,” was recorded
  at Acme Comedy Club in Minneapolis\, Minnesota and was released in April 
 of 2024.
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/361515
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic, BloomingtonArts.Today, Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncountyplayhouse": "https://browncountyplayhouse.org/event/arsenic-and-old-lace-live-theatre/2026-10-10/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncountyplayhouse
X-SOURCE:Brown County Playhouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T220000
DTSTAMP:20260924T191417Z
CREATED:20260617T153600Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T191417Z
UID:10001512-1791660600-1791669600@browncountyplayhouse.org
SUMMARY:Arsenic and Old Lace [Live Theatre]
DESCRIPTION:Drama critic Mortimer Brewster’s engagement announcement is upended when he discovers a corpse in his elderly aunts’ window seat. Mortimer rushes to tell Abby and Martha before they stumble upon the body themselves\, only to learn that the two old women aren’t just aware of the dead man in their parlor\, they killed him! Between his aunts’ penchant for poisoning wine\, a brother who thinks he’s Teddy Roosevelt\, and another brother using plastic surgery to hide from the police – not to mention Mortimer’s own hesitancy about marriage – it’ll be a miracle if Mortimer makes it to his wedding. Arsenic and Old Lace is a classic dark comedy about the only thing more deadly than poison: family. \n\nAbby Brewster: Becky Stapf\nMartha Brewster: Amy Frazer\nRev. Dr. Harper: Mike Harold\nTeddy Brewster: Jerry Maguire\nOfficer Brophy: Mark Webber\nOfficer Klein: Devon Davis\nElaine Harper: Shaun Ancelet\nMortimer Brewster: Ben Sledge\nMr. Gibbs: Jackson Flora\nJonathan Brewster: Horace Tucker\nDr. Einstein: Steve Scott\nOfficer O’Hara: Robert Stevens\nLt. Rooney: Mark Owens\nMr. Witherspoon: Harold Crooks\nDirector: Susan Rardin\nAsst. Director: Leslie L Clauss\n\n\nBUY TICKETS - Friday Oct 2 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Saturday Oct 3 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Sunday Oct 4 - 2:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Friday Oct 9 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Saturday Oct 10 - 7:30pm\n\nBUY TICKETS - Sunday Oct 11 - 2:30pm
URL:https://browncountyplayhouse.org/event/arsenic-and-old-lace-live-theatre/2026-10-10/
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S. Van Buren St\, Nashville\, IN\, 47448\, United States
CATEGORIES:Featured Event,Live Shows,Play,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncountyplayhouse.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2026-Arsenic-and-Old-Lace-WEB.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Brown County State Park": "on.in.gov/BrownCountySP"}
X-SOURCE-ID:localist_brown_county_sp
SUMMARY:New Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T213000
UID:31abe7039d462b6ed61197c11913d852@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Full Moons occur when the Moon is fully illuminated by the Sun
 \, allowing viewers on Earth to see the full circle. It&#39\;s typically t
 he brightest night of the month. The New Moon is the darkest night of the 
 month\, when dark side of the Moon faces Earth. We&#39\;re going on a hike
  on the darkest night of the month! We will meet at the Park Office/Fire T
 ower Parking lot at 7:30pm to hike Trail 10. Please note Trail 10 should b
 e considered very rugged in the dark and involves hiking from one of the h
 ighest elevations in the park to one of the lowest. The route is 2.2 miles
  and will take about two hours. Red flashlights help us preserve night vis
 ion. We have some to lend out\, but it is wise to bring your own if you ha
 ve one. Hike cancellation policy: Hikes will be cancelled if there is ligh
 tning\, temperatures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above
  105 degrees Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gate
 houses will be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-9
 88-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Park office\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvill
 e\, IN 
URL:on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
