DESCRIPTION:The Borns Jewish Studies Program presents the culminating conc
 ert of Memory Transformed: Materials of Heritage in Jewish Eastern Europea
 n Life\, featuring The Sway Machinery and The Immortal Khazntes.  Bringing
  together musicians whose work engages deeply with Jewish musical traditio
 ns\, the concert explores the continuing life and transformation of Easter
 n European Jewish music through contemporary performance.  The concert con
 cludes a full day of Memory Transformed programming at Indiana University 
 Bloomington\, including a symposium on Jewish cultural heritage and materi
 al culture\, an afternoon reception at the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, and gu
 ided museum tours.Free and open to the public. Registration is encouraged 
 but not required\; no ticket is required for entry.  Please visit the Memo
 ry Transformed event webpage for the latest program and location informati
 on.
