BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_bloomington_in_gov_1rosks8nont4ebaq41tfgg8v7g_group_calendar_google_com
SUMMARY:Fitness in the Park: Tai Chi
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T200000
DTSTAMP:20260926T045228Z
UID:7m5j0hm72pkpu4ok03hv356hmk@google.com__20261012
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260814T181845Z
DESCRIPTION:<h3><b>Tai Chi in the Park</b></h3><ul><li><strong><b>Admissio
 n:</b></strong> $10 per person per class\; no pre-registration required. 
 Pay with card or cash on site.</li><li><strong><b>Day:</b></strong> Monda
 ys\, Sept. 14-Oct. 12</li><li><strong><b>Time: </b></strong>7-8 p.m.</li>
 <li><strong><b>Accessibility:</b></strong> Classes take place on the Swit
 chyard Park Main Stage. The stage is a smooth\, concrete surface accessibl
 e via ramp or stairs.</li><li><address><p>Switchyard Park\, Main Stage<br>
 1601 S. Rogers St.<br>Bloomington\, IN 47403</p></address></li></ul><p>Tai
  Chi is a moving meditation in the form of a series of gentle exercises to
  create harmony and cultivate our inner life energy (qi) to flow smoothly 
 and powerfully through the body. This is a spiritual experience\, as much 
 as a physical one.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260814T183721Z
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Parks and Recreation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_sanshinji_org_3q9maq1gaa99bpu6da81ibrl7g
SUMMARY:Ryaku fusatsu ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T200000
DTSTAMP:20260926T045231Z
UID:2p9qo98rcrv23pdlkeu2601ogh@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260916T143455Z
DESCRIPTION:<table><tbody><tr><td>Ryaku fusatsu is our monthly ceremony o
 f recognizing and renewing our aspiration to embody the <a href="https://
 sanshin-source.weebly.com/precepts.html" target="_blank"><u><u>bodhisattva
  precepts</u></u></a> throughout our lives. We carry out this ceremony on
  the Monday evening closest to the 15th of each month (except Feb &amp\; A
 ug)\, beginning at 7 pm.<br><br>​All are welcome\, in-person and <a hre
 f="https://www.sanshinji.org/virtual-practice.html" target="_blank"><u><u>
 virtually</u></u></a>\, whether or not you've formally received precepts.
  </td></tr></tbody></table><br><strong><em>If attending in person\, pleas
 e show up by 6:50 pm\, to allow enough time for offering incense and purif
 ying rakusu or okesa (if you have one) before the ceremony.</em></strong><
 br><br><b><u>RF dates coming up:</u></b><ul><li>Oct 12</li><li>Nov 16</li>
