CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:This workshop introduces the core concepts behind mapping data
  to pitch\, tempo\, and timbre\, and demonstrates a few accessible tools f
 or turning a dataset into an audio track. We'll work through a simple exam
 ple together so participants can hear how sonification reveals structure i
 n time-series or other sequential data. GUI interfaces will be used so no 
 musical or coding background required—though we'll point to R and Python
  libraries for those who want to go further.__________  New to research\, 
 new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about resea
 rch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join u
 s for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching with
  data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder req
 uirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Re
 search Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for
  researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration
 .  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Servi
 ces team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to ch
 eck back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T211731Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2403818-data-sonification
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">This workshop i
 ntroduces the core concepts behind mapping data to pitch\, tempo\, and tim
 bre\, and demonstrates a few accessible tools for turning a dataset into a
 n audio track. We'll work through a simple example together so participant
 s can hear how sonification reveals structure in time-series or other sequ
 ential data. GUI interfaces will be used so no musical or coding backgroun
 d required—though we'll point to R and Python libraries for those who wa
 nt to go further.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:fal
 se\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&quot\;335
 559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</spa
 n></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested
  in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of th
 e Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through t
 he basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing yo
 ur data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.</p><p>
   Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus
  partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessio
 ns may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, please c
 ontact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto:resda
 ta@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regularly\
 , as new sessions are added!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  IU Libraries Research Data Services: <a hr
 ef="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2403818
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1920\,1920/31615_fall_into_research_livewhal
 e_avatar.rev.1785270700.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IS-ONLINE:1
X-LIVEWHALE-ONLINE-TYPE:Online only
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p><span class="TextRun SCXW145383888 BCX2" lang="EN-U
 S" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="none"><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW14
 5383888 BCX2">Data sonification is the practice of translating data into s
 ound\, offering an alternative way to explore patterns\, trends\, and anom
 alies that visualizations can miss.</span></span></p>
