X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Cinema": "https://events.iu.edu/cinemaiub/event/2425023-faust-wlive-music-friday-night-frights", "Pillar Arts Community Calendar": "https://tockify.com/bloomington.arts.calendar/detail/2448/1791932400000"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 81": "https://events.iu.edu/cinemaiub/event/2425023-faust-wlive-music-friday-night-frights"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_81
X-SOURCE:IU Cinema, Pillar Arts Community Calendar
DTSTART:20261013T230000Z
DTEND:20261014T000000Z
LOCATION:IU CINEMA
GEO:39.168613;-86.517376
SUMMARY:Faust w/live music | Friday Night Frights
DESCRIPTION:The Ufa-produced\, silent fantasy film starring Emil Jannings
  that is a hallmark of Murnau's oeuvre and follows the demon Mephisto as 
 he wagers with God that he can corrupt a mortal man's soul. [107 min\; dr
 ama\, fantasy\, horror\; German intertitles with English translation]  Th
 e film will be accompanied by a live score from Minneapolis' ten thousand
  lakes (xkl). ten thousand lakes are Peter Bruhn (percussive and electron
 ic instruments and noises) and Steven Larsen (stringed and electronic ins
 truments and noises). Their influences are numerous\, and not limited to 
 music alone. Visual art\, film\, dance\, poetry\, and literature all info
 rm their approach to creativity\, as does formative years performing in a
  European-based shoe-gaze band and an indie-rock band in the Midwest. xkl
  regularly composes and performs scores to accompany features accompanyin
 g avantgarde and experimental films from the first half of the 20th centu
 ry.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Ufa-produced\, silent fantasy film 
 starring Emil Jannings that is a hallmark of Murnau's oeuvre and follows 
 the demon Mephisto as he wagers with God that he can corrupt a mortal man
 's soul. [107 min\; drama\, fantasy\, horror\; German intertitles with En
 glish translation]</p><p>  The film will be accompanied by a live score f
 rom Minneapolis' ten thousand lakes (xkl). ten thousand lakes are Peter B
 ruhn (percussive and electronic instruments and noises) and Steven Larsen
  (stringed and electronic instruments and noises). Their influences are n
 umerous\, and not limited to music alone. Visual art\, film\, dance\, poe
 try\, and literature all inform their approach to creativity\, as does fo
 rmative years performing in a European-based shoe-gaze band and an indie-
 rock band in the Midwest. xkl regularly composes and performs scores to a
 ccompany features accompanying avantgarde and experimental films from the
  first half of the 20th century.</p>
