DESCRIPTION:Kick off theGlobal Competencies Skills Development Serieswith 
 an exclusive\, small-group evening networking dinner and candid career con
 versation featuring Foreign Service veteran and former Senior Executive Se
 rvice (SES) leaderPaula Reed Lynch. Drop by. You do not have to stay for t
 he whole event. Open to all staff\, faculty\, students\, and the public.Mo
 ving beyond standard Q&amp\;A panels\, this dinner offers students direct 
 access to a top international policy leader who managed over$4 Billionin g
 lobal humanitarian aid and led UN delegations. Enjoy a catered dinner whil
 e discussing high-impact career pathways in international affairs\, govern
 ment service\, global NGOs\, and multilateral diplomacy.What You'll Get Ou
 t of It (Why Attend?)Direct Access &amp\; Mentorship:Engage in an intimate
  roundtable setting with a seasoned executive who served nearly five decad
 es on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy.Unfiltered Career Insights:As
 k your real questions about navigating Foreign Service careers\, policy in
 tegration across USAID &amp\; the Department of State\, and entry points i
 nto global non-profit sectors.High-Impact Networking:Connect with student 
 leaders\, fellowship recipients\, and peers across HLS\, O'Neill\, Cyberse
 curity\, and Public Policy majors.Key NACE Competencies Addressed:Career &
 amp\; Self-Development\, Professionalism\, Communication\, and Equity &amp
 \; Inclusion.  Meet the Guest Speaker - Paula Reed Lynchspent nearly five 
 decades on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy and international relief
 .Serving 14 years in the Senior Executive Service within the Department of
  State's Bureau of Population\, Refugees\, and Migration (PRM)\, Paula ove
 rsaw budgets exceeding $4 billion for global disaster and refugee assistan
 ce.  Career Highlights: First American Rapporteur for the UN High Commissi
 oner for Refugees (UNHCR).Led interagency strategy across the Department o
 f State and USAID.Developed global benchmarks for refugee protection\, inc
 luding work on the SPHERE Standards.Recipient of the Secretary of State's 
 Career Achievement Award.
