CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
DESCRIPTION: \n\nPowering the Alliance: Energy\, Minerals\, and the Race t
 o Break China's Grip on Asia's Supply Chains\nDr. William Chou — Senior F
 ellow and Deputy Director\, Japan Chair\, Hudson Institute\nChina process
 es 90 percent of the world's rare earths and has twice cut off supply to 
 Japan to win a political argument. It controls the inputs behind everythi
 ng from electric vehicles to precision munitions. Dr. William Chou of the
  Hudson Institute explains how Beijing built that leverage\, what it cost
 s America and its allies\, and what Washington and Tokyo are now spending
  hundreds of billions of dollars to undo. From Alaskan gas to rare earth 
 magnets to the power plants behind the AI boom\, this is the competition 
 that will decide who sets the terms in the Indo-Pacific.\nHosted by the A
 lexander Hamilton Society at Indiana University. Free and open to the pub
 lic.\n\n\nHosted by: The Alexander Hamilton Society at Indiana University
  \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.e
 du/event/12803024
DTEND:20261015T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260926T045204Z
DTSTART:20261015T220000Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, FA 102
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:AHS Speaker Series: William Chou on "Energy\, Minerals\, and the R
 ace to Break China's Grip on Asia's Supply Chains"
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12803024
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12803024
X-HOSTS:The Alexander Hamilton Society at Indiana University
