SUMMARY:MVP LSAT Bootcamp with Lawgic Prep
DTSTART:20261017T143000Z
DTEND:20261017T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260916T101758Z
UID:20261017T143000Z-2419899@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261017T143000Z
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Training, non-credit
  classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:The Maurer Vision Program is partnering with Lawgic Prep to ho
 st a free three-day LSAT Readiness Boot Camp on October 6\, 8 and 9\, foll
 owed by a full timed mock LSAT on Saturday\, October 10\, and then a revie
 w session to cover frequently missed diagnostic questions. Led by Lawgic P
 rep co-founder Zach Goldberg (172 LSAT)\, the sessions cover the law schoo
 l application\, the foundational logic the test uses\, and select Logical 
 Reasoning and Reading Comprehension question types\, with real LSAT questi
 ons worked live. No prior LSAT experience is needed\, and everyone who att
 ends receives a discount on Lawgic Prep's services. Bring a laptop and wha
 tever you take notes with\, create a free account at lawgicprep.org before
  the first session\, and register at the link below.  This week\, we are b
 uilding the last deck and session handouts.  Register by October 5th.&#160
 \;
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T162149Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2419899-mvp-lsat-bootcamp-with-lawg
 ic-prep
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Maurer Vision Program is partnering 
 with Lawgic Prep to host a free three-day LSAT Readiness Boot Camp on Octo
 ber 6\, 8 and 9\, followed by a full timed mock LSAT on Saturday\, October
  10\, and then a review session to cover frequently missed diagnostic ques
 tions. Led by Lawgic Prep co-founder Zach Goldberg (172 LSAT)\, the sessio
 ns cover the law school application\, the foundational logic the test uses
 \, and select Logical Reasoning and Reading Comprehension question types\,
  with real LSAT questions worked live. No prior LSAT experience is needed\
 , and everyone who attends receives a discount on Lawgic Prep's services. 
 Bring a laptop and whatever you take notes with\, create a free account at
  lawgicprep.org before the first session\, and register at the link below.
 <br /><br />  This week\, we are building the last deck and session handou
 ts.</p><p>  Register by October 5th.&#160\;</p>
