BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2417427-the-cost-of-values-what-should-libraries-pay-for"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:The Cost of Value(s): What Should Libraries Pay For?
DTSTART:20261019T140000Z
DTEND:20261019T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T144704Z
UID:20261019T140000Z-2417427@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261019T140000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,3200/32496_oa_week_2026_livewhale.rev.1789410307.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Every subscription renewed\, publishing agreement signed\, inf
 rastructure project supported\, or service discontinued helps shape the sc
 holarly communication ecosystem—for better or for worse.  But making spe
 nding decisions that reflect library values is difficult. Libraries must m
 eet their campuses' needs while operating within finite budgets and pursui
 ng broader commitments to affordability\, equity\, and the long-term healt
 h of scholarly communication.  This panel will bring together librarians w
 ith expertise in collections and acquisitions strategy\, academic engageme
 nt\, and scholarly communication to explore how libraries can make spendin
 g decisions that are fiscally responsible\, responsive to local needs\, an
 d aligned with broader professional and institutional values. How can libr
 aries serve their campuses while also helping build a more equitable\, aff
 ordable\, open\, and sustainable scholarly communication system?PanelistsR
 achel Caldwell (https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachel-caldwell-947a10247/)\, 
 Head\, Academic Engagement\, University of Massachusetts Amherst Libraries
   Erin Gallagher (https://experts.ufl.edu/experts/erin.gallagher/)\, Chair
 \, Acquisitions &amp\; Discovery Services\, University of Florida Librarie
 s  Laura Hanscom (https://libraries.mit.edu/scholarly/about/)\, Head\, Sch
 olarly Communications &amp\; Collections Strategy\, MIT Libraries  Moderat
 orWilla Liburd (https://libraries.indiana.edu/willa-liburd)\, Research Imp
 act &amp\; Open Scholarship Librarian\, IU Bloomington Libraries
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T154805Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2417427-the-cost-of-values-what-
 should-libraries-pay-for
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Every subscription renewed\, publishing 
 agreement signed\, infrastructure project supported\, or service discontin
 ued helps shape the scholarly communication ecosystem—for better or for 
 worse.</p><p>  But making spending decisions that reflect library values i
 s difficult. Libraries must meet their campuses' needs while operating wit
 hin finite budgets and pursuing broader commitments to affordability\, equ
 ity\, and the long-term health of scholarly communication.</p><p>  This pa
 nel will bring together librarians with expertise in collections and acqui
 sitions strategy\, academic engagement\, and scholarly communication to ex
 plore how libraries can make spending decisions that are fiscally responsi
 ble\, responsive to local needs\, and aligned with broader professional an
 d institutional values. How can libraries serve their campuses while also 
 helping build a more equitable\, affordable\, open\, and sustainable schol
 arly communication system?</p><p><strong>Panelists</strong></p><ul><li><a 
 href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachel-caldwell-947a10247/">Rachel Caldw
 ell</a>\, Head\, Academic Engagement\, University of Massachusetts Amherst
  Libraries  </li><li><a href="https://experts.ufl.edu/experts/erin.gallagh
 er/">Erin Gallagher</a>\, Chair\, Acquisitions &amp\; Discovery Services\,
  University of Florida Libraries  </li><li><a href="https://libraries.mit.
 edu/scholarly/about/">Laura Hanscom</a>\, Head\, Scholarly Communications 
 &amp\; Collections Strategy\, MIT Libraries  </li></ul><p><strong>Moderato
 r</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/willa-liburd"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Willa Liburd</a>\, Research Impact &amp\; 
