SUMMARY:New York Program Info Session
DTSTART:20261019T160000Z
DTEND:20261019T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260916T182324Z
UID:20261019T160000Z-2420145@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261019T160000Z
CATEGORIES:Career development
DESCRIPTION:New York Program Info Session  Are you interested in spending 
 your summer in New York? CSO is hosting an info session for you to learn a
 bout IU Maurer's alumni-run program.  For those interested in exploring ca
 reers in New York and in the public sector. IU Alumnus and Adjunct Profess
 or Terrance Stroud has developed relationships with a number of public sec
 tor employers\, including the New York City Bar\, the New York Department 
 of Education\, and Brooklyn College's General Counsel's Office\, and assis
 ts students with these opportunities or other public sector opportunities.
  Professor Stroud also organizes weekly networking events where participan
 ts can connect with and learn from alumni and other practitioners working 
 in a variety of settings in New York City\, including the judiciary\, the 
 United Nations\, federal agencies\, politics\, academia\, non-profits\, an
 d a DA's Office. These positions are unpaid\, but public interest position
 s will qualify the participant to apply for PILF and other summer public i
 nterest funding through Maurer. Students who obtain positions in New York 
 through other means are also welcome to join the program for its networkin
 g and educational benefits.  Learn more about the New York Program and Pro
 fessor Stroud here: https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/ (h
 ttps://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/)  RSVP by October 11th 
 to attend.&#160\;
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T131641Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2420145-new-york-program-info-sessi
 on
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  New York Program Info Session<br />  Are
  you interested in spending your summer in New York? CSO is hosting an inf
 o session for you to learn about IU Maurer's alumni-run program.<br /><br 
 />  For those interested in exploring careers in New York and in the publi
 c sector. IU Alumnus and Adjunct Professor Terrance Stroud has developed r
 elationships with a number of public sector employers\, including the New 
 York City Bar\, the New York Department of Education\, and Brooklyn Colleg
 e's General Counsel's Office\, and assists students with these opportuniti
 es or other public sector opportunities. Professor Stroud also organizes w
 eekly networking events where participants can connect with and learn from
  alumni and other practitioners working in a variety of settings in New Yo
 rk City\, including the judiciary\, the United Nations\, federal agencies\
 , politics\, academia\, non-profits\, and a DA's Office. These positions a
 re unpaid\, but public interest positions will qualify the participant to 
 apply for PILF and other summer public interest funding through Maurer. St
 udents who obtain positions in New York through other means are also welco
 me to join the program for its networking and educational benefits.</p><p>
   Learn more about the New York Program and Professor Stroud here: <a href
 ="https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/">https://www.legalev
 olution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/</a></p><p>  RSVP by October 11th to atten
 d.&#160\;</p>
