BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 64": "https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2410793-sit-stay-plan-estate-planning-for-pets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_64
SUMMARY:Sit\, Stay\, Plan: Estate Planning for Pets
DTSTART:20261019T160000Z
DTEND:20261019T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260908T124657Z
UID:20261019T160000Z-2410793@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261019T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Real Estate and Estate Planning Association (REEPA) a
 nd the Student Animal Legal Defense Fund (SALDF) on Monday\, October 19\, 
 for a presentation by Lisa Adler ('04) exploring the fascinating intersect
 ion of estate planning and animal law.  Once treated as property\, pets no
 w have evolving legal protections and estate-planning options. Pets may be
  family\, but what happens to them when their owners become incapacitated 
 or die? The answer is more complicated (and more legally interesting) than
  you might think. Learn how attorneys can help clients plan for their pets
 ' futures\, and explore the evolving laws and practical challenges surroun
 ding pets and estate planning.  Whether you're interested in estate planni
 ng\, animal law\, or simply curious about an unexpected and fascinating ar
 ea of legal practice\, come join us! Lunch will be provided to those who R
 SVP by 5pm on October 18!
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T163130Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2410793-sit-stay-plan-estate-planni
 ng-for-pets
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the Real Estate and Estate Planning
  Association (REEPA) and the Student Animal Legal Defense Fund (SALDF) on 
 Monday\, October 19\, for a presentation by Lisa Adler ('04) exploring the
  fascinating intersection of estate planning and animal law.<br /><br />  
 Once treated as property\, pets now have evolving legal protections and es
 tate-planning options. Pets may be family\, but what happens to them when 
 their owners become incapacitated or die? The answer is more complicated (
 and more legally interesting) than you might think. Learn how attorneys ca
 n help clients plan for their pets' futures\, and explore the evolving law
 s and practical challenges surrounding pets and estate planning.<br /><br 
 />  Whether you're interested in estate planning\, animal law\, or simply 
 curious about an unexpected and fascinating area of legal practice\, come 
 join us! Lunch will be provided to those who RSVP by 5pm on October 18!</p
 >
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Elly Slevin&#160\;<br />\n  Event Organize
 r<br />\n  Student Animal Legal Defense Fund (SALDF)&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2410793
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Real Estate and Estate Planning Association|Student Anima
 l Legal Defense Fund
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Maurer School of Law
