X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/birds-in-books"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:An ornithology pop-up exhibition
DTSTART:20261020T180000Z
DTEND:20261020T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T121647Z
UID:20261020T180000Z-2417196@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261020T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,600,600/32451_ornithology_pop-up_livewhale_avatar.rev.178
 9052157.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Whether locally or globally\, birds are a critical part of Ear
 th's ecosystems. This event is a celebration of birds as they appear in hi
 storical books and manuscripts.  Visitors can page through the Lilly Libra
 ry's dazzling collection of ornithology materials and learn how to get mor
 e involved in local bird conservation efforts. Visitors will have a chance
  to get up close and personal with one of the great treasures of the Lilly
  Library—the Double Elephant Folio edition of John James Audubon's Birds
  of America\, featuring life-sized\, hand-colored engravings of Audubon's 
 captivating ornithological studies. Indiana University's own Audubon exper
 t\, Dr. Christoph Irmscher\, will be present to talk about his research an
 d writings on Audubon and natural history.Larks\, Loons\, and Lorikeets at
  the Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition&#160\;is free and open to bir
 d nerds of all ages.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T162754Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/birds-in-books
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Whether locally o
 r globally\, birds are a critical part of Earth's ecosystems. This event i
 s a celebration of birds as they appear in historical books and manuscript
 s.</p><p>  Visitors can page through the Lilly Library's dazzling collecti
 on of ornithology materials and learn how to get more involved in local bi
 rd conservation efforts. Visitors will have a chance to get up close and p
 ersonal with one of the great treasures of the Lilly Library—the Double 
 Elephant Folio edition of John James Audubon's <em>Birds of America</em>\,
  featuring life-sized\, hand-colored engravings of Audubon's captivating o
 rnithological studies. Indiana University's own Audubon expert\, Dr. Chris
 toph Irmscher\, will be present to talk about his research and writings on
  Audubon and natural history.</p><p><em>Larks\, Loons\, and Lorikeets at t
 he Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition</em>&#160\;is free and open to 
 bird nerds of all ages.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Lilly Library</strong><br />\n  <a
  href="mailto:liblilly@iu.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">liblilly@iu.
 edu</a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2417196
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,600\,600/32451_ornithology_pop-up_livewhale_
 avatar.rev.1789052157.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">\n  Join us at IU Libraries 
 Lilly Library on Tuesday\, October 20 from 2–4pm for <em>Larks\, Loons\,
  and Lorikeets at the Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition</em> in part
 nership with the Sassafras Audubon Society of Indiana!\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute, IU Bloomington Libraries
END:VEVENT
