X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Eskenazi School of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/abelardo-morell-artist-talk", "Architecture + Design": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/abelardo-morell-artist-talk", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/abelardo-morell-artist-talk"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/abelardo-morell-artist-talk"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Abelardo Morell: The Universe Next Door
DTSTART:20261022T213000Z
DTEND:20261022T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260818T132925Z
UID:20261022T213000Z-2385082@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261022T213000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,644,800/32022_RS23041_2025.100_view_1_dig_2.rev.178698330
 4.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:5:30-6:30 PM\, Artist talk and Q&amp\;A\,&#160\;Martin Commons
 \, second floor6:30-7:00 PM\, Enjoy Morell's photographs in The Photograph
 ic Reflex\, Featured Exhibition\, first floorAbelardo Morell's photographs
  reach through art history to one of the earliest predecessors of the medi
 um\, the camera obscura. In conjunction with the featured exhibitionThe Ph
 otographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection (https:
 //artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-d
 eprez.html)\, the photographer will speak about his artistic practice and 
 delve into his remarkable career. He has continually returned to the funda
 mental mechanics of light and vision\, using them to transform ordinary ro
 oms and landscapes into sites of quiet revelation.To make his most celebra
 ted body of work\, Morell darkens an entire room and leaves a single small
  opening in a window. Light passes through that aperture and projects an i
 nverted image of the outside world onto the interior walls. City streets\,
  trees\, and skylines appear suspended across beds\, ceilings\, and wallpa
 per. Morell then photographs this projection\, joining interior and exteri
 or in a single frame. The process follows the basic laws of optics\, yet t
 he result feels magical and imaginative\, as the world outside settles ins
 ide the room. This sustained investigation earned him a Guggenheim Fellows
 hip in 1993 and remains central to his practice.Artist Bio:Abelardo Morell
  was born in Havana\, Cuba in 1948. He immigrated to the United States wit
 h his parents in 1962.  Morell received his undergraduate degree from Bo
 wdoin College and his MFA from The Yale University School of Art. He was p
 rofessor of Photography at the Massachusetts College of Art and Design in 
 Boston from 1983 to 2010. His work is held in leading public collections w
 orldwide and a major retrospective\, The Universe Next Door\, opened at 
 the Art Institute of Chicago in 2013 and traveled to the Getty Museum in L
 os Angeles and the High Museum of Art in Atlanta.https://www.abelardomorel
 l.net/
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260824T141449Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/abelardo-morell-artist-talk
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="auto"><span class="No
 rmalTextRun SCXW15750192 BCX4"><strong>5:30-6:30 PM\,</strong> Artist talk
  and Q&amp\;A\,</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW15750192 BCX4">&#160\
 ;Martin Commons</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW15750192 BCX4">\, sec
 ond floor</span></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto"><span class="Norm
 alTextRun SCXW15750192 BCX4"><strong>6:30-7:00 PM\,</strong> Enjoy Morell'
 s photographs in <em>The Photographic Reflex</em>\, Featured Exhibition\, 
 first floor</span></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Abelardo Morell
 's photographs reach through art history to one of the earliest predecesso
 rs of the medium\, the camera obscura. In conjunction with the featured ex
 hibition</span><i><span data-contrast="auto"><a href="https://artmuseum.in
 diana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html" ta
 rget="_blank" rel="noopener">The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and Jo
 hn C. DePrez Jr. Collection</a></span></i><span data-contrast="auto">\, th
 e photographer will speak about his artistic practice and delve into his r
 emarkable career. He has continually returned to the fundamental mechanics
  of light and vision\, using them to transform ordinary rooms and landscap
 es into sites of quiet revelation.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span>
 </p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span>
 </p><p><span data-contrast="auto">To make his most celebrated body of work
 \, Morell darkens an entire room and leaves a single small opening in a wi
 ndow. Light passes through that aperture and projects an inverted image of
  the outside world onto the interior walls. City streets\, trees\, and sky
 lines appear suspended across beds\, ceilings\, and wallpaper. Morell then
  photographs this projection\, joining interior and exterior in a single f
 rame. The process follows the basic laws of optics\, yet the result feels 
 magical and imaginative\, as the world outside settles inside the room. Th
 is sustained investigation earned him a Guggenheim Fellowship in 1993 and 
 remains central to his practice.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></
 p><p><strong>Artist Bio:</strong></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Abelard
 o Morell was born in Havana\, Cuba in 1948. He immigrated to the United St
 ates with his parents in 1962.  Morell received his undergraduate degree
  from Bowdoin College and his MFA from The Yale University School of Art. 
 He was professor of Photography at the Massachusetts College of Art and De
 sign in Boston from 1983 to 2010. His work is held in leading public colle
 ctions worldwide and a major retrospective\, </span><i><span data-contra
 st="auto">The Universe Next Door</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">\, o
 pened at the Art Institute of Chicago in 2013 and traveled to the Getty Mu
 seum in Los Angeles and the High Museum of Art in Atlanta.</span><span dat
 a-ccp-props="{}"></span></p><p><a href="https://www.abelardomorell.net/"><
 span data-contrast="none">https://www.abelardomorell.net/</span></a><span 
 data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;
 :0\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:278}"></span></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Emily Zarse<br />\n  Public Experiences Ma
 nager\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
