 a></span><span class="s1">is an<strong>&#160\;</strong>eye-opening and awa
 rd-winning documentary about three survivors of abuse fighting for their l
 ives and how the legal system betrayed them.&#160\;</span></p><p class="p1
 "><span class="s1">These women paid a steep price with long prison sentenc
 es\, lost time with loved ones\, and painful memories. Formerly incarcerat
 ed survivor-advocate Kim Dadou Brown\, who met her wife while incarcerated
 \, is a driving force in the passage of New York's Domestic Violence Survi
 vors Justice Act (DVSJA)\, a new law meant to prevent survivors from recei
 ving harsh prison sentences for their acts of survival. Nikki Addimando\, 
 a mother of two young children\, suffered the consequences when a judge di
