SUMMARY:Lecture: "Opportunity or Threat? Environmental\, Social\, and Gove
 rnance (ESG) Transformation in Polish Companies" with Monika Foltyn-Zarych
 ta
DTSTART:20261023T180000Z
DTEND:20261023T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T153747Z
UID:20261023T180000Z-2402263@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261023T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/181/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2812/32151_Monika_edit.rev.1787580502.jpg
DESCRIPTION:European Union regulations are pushing companies beyond symbol
 ic ESG compliance and reporting towards genuine socially responsible trans
 formation. However\, should Polish firms invest more in ESG transformation
 ? Will consumers reward such investments through their purchasing decision
 s? And how will financial markets respond to companies making these invest
 ments? I will explore these questions in my lecture.  Monika Foltyn-Zarych
 ta\, Ph.D.\, is an Associate Professor at the University of Economics in K
 atowice\, Poland. Her research focuses on climate change\, sustainability\
 , and the ethical dimensions of investment decision-making\, with particul
 ar emphasis on intergenerational justice\, long-term discounting\, and cos
 t-benefit analysis. She is currently a Visiting Scholar at the Ostrom Work
 shop at Indiana University.  Cosponsored by the Polish Studies Center and 
 the Byrnes Institute (REEI)
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260831T193747Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2391957-lecture-opportunity-or-threa
 t-environmental-social
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  European Union regulations are pushing c
 ompanies beyond symbolic ESG compliance and reporting towards genuine soci
 ally responsible transformation. However\, should Polish firms invest more
  in ESG transformation? Will consumers reward such investments through the
 ir purchasing decisions? And how will financial markets respond to compani
 es making these investments? I will explore these questions in my lecture.
 </p><p>  Monika Foltyn-Zarychta\, Ph.D.\, is an Associate Professor at the
  University of Economics in Katowice\, Poland. Her research focuses on cli
 mate change\, sustainability\, and the ethical dimensions of investment de
 cision-making\, with particular emphasis on intergenerational justice\, lo
 ng-term discounting\, and cost-benefit analysis. She is currently a Visiti
 ng Scholar at the Ostrom Workshop at Indiana University.</p><p>  Cosponsor
 ed by the Polish Studies Center and the Byrnes Institute (REEI)</p>
