 -at-t" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>And So I Stayed</em></a> will sc
 reen at the IU Cinema on Saturday\, October 24 at 7:00 PM. **</p><p><span 
 data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody"><strong>Natalie Pattillo</strong> is an
  award-winning documentary filmmaker\, writer and journalist whose work ex
 plores education\, child care access\, gender-based violence\, food and cu
 lture. Her work has appeared in The New York Times\, MSNBC\, VICE\, New Yo
 rk Magazine\, Al Jazeera America\, Salon and beyond. In 2020\, she receive
 d the Media Award from the National Coalition Against Domestic Violence. S
 he was also named a Faculty News Champion by the Center for Community News
  at the University of Vermont for her work supporting student journalism a
 nd rebuilding local news.</span></p><p>  Natalie was the co-director\, wri
 ter and producer of <em><a class="external" title="Original URL: https://w
 ww.nytimes.com/2021/06/11/movies/domestic-violence-law.html. Click or tap 
 if you trust this link." href="https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.
 com/?url=https:%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2021%2F06%2F11%2Fmovies%2Fdomestic-
 violence-law.html&amp\;data=05%7C02%7Cmrolfes%40iu.edu%7C68533c4a975c40213
 5b208def48f0787%7C1113be34aed14d00ab4bcdd02510be91%7C1%7C0%7C6392170923796
