 yPnKf38%3D&amp\;reserved=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data
 -auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="1">Writing for My Mother</a></em>\, 
 a documentary and book project exploring literacy in the United States\, t
 he communities that have been excluded from educational opportunities and 
 what becomes possible in people's lives and for our democracy when those b
 arriers are broken down.</p><p>  Natalie lives in Providence\, Rhode Islan
 d\, with her husband and three children. In her free time\, she can usuall
 y be found gardening\, knitting\, reading<span class="x_gmail_default">\,<
 /span> or <span class="x_gmail_default">taking unhurried walks.</span></p>
