SUMMARY: Pythagorean Theorem Day
DESCRIPTION:Fun Fact: Pythagoras was kind of a radical dude in his day — 
 he ran a secret society of math-obsessed mystics\, believed numbers held 
 the key to the universe\, and mixed geometry with music\, philosophy\, an
 d a little bit of showmanship. For Pythagoras\, math was mind-blowing.\n\
 nBlow your mind at WonderLab this Pythagorean Theorem Day! Explore hands-
 on triangle challenges\, math-inspired art\, and puzzles throughout the m
 useum\, and discover how one ancient theorem still shows up everywhere — 
 from architecture to nature to the numbers on today's calendar.\n\nEmbrac
 e the endless creativity of mathematics. Join us at WonderLab for Pythago
 rean Theorem Day — a once-in-a-lifetime date when the calendar does the m
 ath for you: 10-24-26 means 10² + 24² = 26².\n\nActivities include:\n\n  
 * Mathematical Story Time — Strega Nona: Exponential Growth\, a math-them
 ed read-aloud.\n  * Pythagorean Pan Pipes — Explore the math behind music
  by building your own pan pipes.\n  * PT Proofs — Hands-on manipulatives 
 of many known proofs of the Pythagorean Theorem\, ready to explore and te
 st yourself.\n  * Math Trail — Follow WonderLab's Math Trail and discover
  math hiding throughout the museum.\n  * Tessellating Magnets — Create yo
 ur own tessellating patterns on a magnetic board\, with step-by-step guid
 ance.\n  * Finding Pythagorean Triples — Use blocks to visually build and
  discover triples like 3-4-5 and 10-24-26.\n  * PT in Art & Architecture 
 — A quilting and design station: use 10x10 squares and 3-4-5 right triang
 les to build your own pattern\, inspired by Bhaskara's classic geometric 
 proof.
CATEGORIES:
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62fb9509b27fd5
 06428328ed/6ab13cb1cd7aa68c2cf01af4/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Fun Fact: Pythagoras was kind of a radical dude in h
 is day — he ran a secret society of math-obsessed mystics\, believed numb
 ers held the key to the...
X-TKF-PROMOTION-BUTTON;label=Learn More;skip_details=false:https://wonder
 lab.org/pythagorean-theorem-day/
LOCATION:WonderLab Museum\,308 W. 4th Street
CREATED:20260921T141826Z
DTSTAMP:20260926T045228Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T141826Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CLASS:PUBLIC
