UID:20261029T160000Z-2416921@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261029T160000Z
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Join the Environmental Futures in the Arts and Humanities Init
 iative for our first 2026-2027 lunch-hour discussion in a series designed 
 to bring together scholars and artists in the arts and humanities whose wo
 rk engages with "Water Ways"—whether through histories of trade\, empire
 \, and exchange\, Indigenous knowledges\, literature\, environmental justi
 ce issues\, and art. Each lunch will feature a panel of faculty who will i
 nformally share their work-in-progress.  Our features speakers for the fal
 l lunch are:  Katina Bitsicas (BioArt\, Media School)  Michelle Del Rio (P
 ublic Health)  Rebecca Lave (Geography)  Teresa Kovacs (Germanic Studies) 
  Ahmed Shams (Media School)
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T160731Z
LOCATION:MAXWELL HALL
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2381160-environmental-futures-cross-
 pollination-luncheon
