 ts and Humanities Initiative for our first 2026-2027 lunch-hour discussion
  in a series designed to bring together scholars and artists in the arts a
 nd humanities whose work engages with "Water Ways"—whether through histo
 ries of trade\, empire\, and exchange\, Indigenous knowledges\, literature
 \, environmental justice issues\, and art. Each lunch will feature a panel
  of faculty who will informally share their work-in-progress.</p><p>  Our 
