X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Brown County Art Guild 2026 Annual Raffle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261030T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261030T220000
DTSTAMP:20260417T142538Z
UID:MEC-d14387be71d9f4739f36dd3051dfb343@browncounty.com__20261030
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 04/f461e264-81fc-43ba-96f8-1ed7cc92b101.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art Events &amp\; Exhibits,Happening,Tournaments &amp\; Games
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260417
DESCRIPTION:Take a chance to win ‘Painters Point’\, a beautiful origin
 al oil painting generously donated by Guild Artist\, Allen Hutton. He stri
 ves to render the fleeting patterns of light and shadow with the simple 
 purpose of preserving the reality of a landscape at a particular moment in
  time and season. Allen has achieved numerous awards and his art can be
  found in both private and corporate collections across the county.   \
 nTickets:  1 for $30\, 2 for $50\, or 5 for $100   \nYour generosity h
 elps the Guild to preserve its historic collection\, promote its award-win
 ning artist members\, and offer workshops and programs throughout the year
 !  \nThe drawing of the winning raffle ticket will be held at 3pm on Sat
 urday\, November 21\, 2026\, at the Guild.  \nThe winner need not be pre
 sent for the drawing.  \nPurchase options: \nIn person at the Guild\, c
 all 812-988-6185 or purchase raffle tickets at:  \nhttps://browncountyar
 tguild.org/product/brown-county-art-guild-annual-raffle/ \n————
 ————————————————————————
 ————————————- \nBrown County Art Guild – PO B
 ox 324 – 48 S. Van Buren St. Nashville\, Indiana 47448 – Ph# 812-9
 88-6185 \n– A not-for-profit organization located in the heart of d
 owntown Nashville\, Indiana. On display throughout its galleries is a priz
 ed collection of historic paintings as well as current works for sale from
  regional award-winning member artists.  Throughout the year\, the Guil
 d offers artist demonstrations\, workshops\, and special exhibits.   \
 nGuild hours: March-December 2026\, Monday – Saturday\, 11 – 5 and Sun
 day\, 12 – 4 or by appointment. \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260629
LOCATION:Brown County Art Guild\, South Van Buren Street\, Nashville\, IN
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Art Guild":MAILTO:admin@bcartguild.org
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/brown-county-art-guild-2026-annual-raff
 le/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 237": "https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376568-embedded-accessible-educational-services-aes"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_237
SUMMARY:Embedded Accessible Educational Services (AES)
DTSTART:20261030T120000Z
DTEND:20261030T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260810T143355Z
UID:20261002T120000Z-2376568@events.iu.edu__20261030
DESCRIPTION:At the LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, we want every student to have t
 he resources they need to thrive. Disabilities come in all shapes and size
 s\, and many are not visible to others. Accessible Educational Services (A
 ES) partners with students to provide accommodations\, support services\, 
 and tools that help create equal access and opportunity at IU.  Kade Padge
 tt\, M.A.\, an AES Access Coordinator\, is available at the LGBTQ+ Culture
  Center every Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. during drop-in advising h
 ours. Whether you're curious about accommodations\, have questions about t
 he process\, or simply want to learn more about available resources\, we i
 nvite you to stop by and chat with Kade about the support options that may
  be available to you.  All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities
 \, educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all members
  of the Indiana University community.
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T171748Z
LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376568-embedded-accessible-educatio
 nal-services-aes
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div><p>    At the LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, we
  want every student to have the resources they need to thrive. Disabilitie
 s come in all shapes and sizes\, and many are not visible to others. Acces
 sible Educational Services (AES) partners with students to provide accommo
 dations\, support services\, and tools that help create equal access and o
 pportunity at IU.  </p><p><strong>Kade Padgett\, M.A.\, an AES Access Coor
 dinator\,</strong> is available at the LGBTQ+ Culture Center every Friday 
 from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. during drop-in advising hours. Whether you're 
 curious about accommodations\, have questions about the process\, or simpl
 y want to learn more about available resources\, we invite you to stop by 
 and chat with Kade about the support options that may be available to you.
   </p><p><strong>All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, edu
 cational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all members of th
 e Indiana University community.</strong></p></div>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2376568
X-LIVEWHALE-REPEATS-UNTIL:2026-12-11 13:00:00
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU LGBTQ+ Culture Center
END:VEVENT
