BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2404999-tommy-kha-ghost-bites-and-other-vietnamese-phrases"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Tommy Kha: Ghost Bites\, and Other Vietnamese Phrases | Lecture
DTSTART:20261030T210000Z
DTEND:20261030T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T110820Z
UID:20261030T210000Z-2404999@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261030T210000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,1152/32325_Tommy-Kha-photo-by-Jay_Amrahs-WEB.rev.17883
 61415.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:A 2025 Guggenheim Fellow\, Kha lives and works between New Yor
 k City and Memphis\, Tennessee\, his birthplace. He holds an M.F.A. in pho
 tography from Yale University\, where he currently teaches.Kha's work is i
 n the collections of MoMA\, SFMoMA\, George Eastman House\, the Guggenheim
  Museum\, and the Virginia Museum of Fine Arts. His first solo museum show
 \, "Other Things Uttered\," was held at the Addison Gallery of American Ar
 t in September 2025.In 2023\, Aperture published his first monograph "Half
 \, Full\, Quarter" following his solo shows "Ghost Bites" and "Má\," an o
 ngoing\, decade-long collaboration between the artist and his mother. Kha'
 s work has also appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, The New Yorker\,
  and The Wall Street Journal as well as Hyperallergic\, Interview\, McSwee
 ney's\, Vice\, Pitchfork\, Southern Cultures\, Dazed\, Foam\, Butt Magazin
 e\, and Miranda July's "We Think Alone."Kha is previously a recipient of t
 he Hayes Prize\, Next Step Award\, Foam Talent\, and NYSCA/NYFA Artist Fel
 low in Photography. He is a former resident at Pioneer Works\, Lighthouse 
 Works\, Kinosaito\, Light Work\, and BAXTER ST (née Camera Club of New Yo
 rk).He has had solo shows at Higher Pictures (which he joined in 2022)\, B
 AXTER ST\, and Blue Sky Gallery. He has taught at the New School and Rutge
 rs University and is a critic at Yale University. Currently\, Kha studies 
 kung fu under Sifu Ken Lo.According to Kha\, he "takes after his great aun
 t\, who 'read too many books and went crazy'." Artist's website:https:
 //tommykha.com (https://tommykha.com)  &#160\;
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T150820Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2404999-tommy-kha-ghost-bites-and
 -other-vietnamese-phrases
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1"><span class="s1">A 2025 Guggenh
 eim Fellow\, Kha lives and works between New York City and Memphis\, Tenne
 ssee\, his birthplace. He holds an M.F.A. in photography from Yale Univers
 ity\, where he currently teaches.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"
 >Kha's work is in the collections of MoMA\, SFMoMA\, George Eastman House\
 , the Guggenheim Museum\, and the Virginia Museum of Fine Arts. His first 
 solo museum show\, "Other Things Uttered\," was held at the Addison Galler
 y of American Art in September 2025.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="
 s1">In 2023\, Aperture published his first monograph "Half\, Full\, Quarte
 r" following his solo shows "Ghost Bites" and "Má\," an ongoing\, decade-
 long collaboration between the artist and his mother. Kha's work has also 
 appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, The New Yorker\, and The Wall St
 reet Journal as well as Hyperallergic\, Interview\, McSweeney's\, Vice\, P
 itchfork\, Southern Cultures\, Dazed\, Foam\, Butt Magazine\, and Miranda 
 July's "We Think Alone."</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">Kha is p
 reviously a recipient of the Hayes Prize\, Next Step Award\, Foam Talent\,
  and NYSCA/NYFA Artist Fellow in Photography. He is a former resident at P
 ioneer Works\, Lighthouse Works\, Kinosaito\, Light Work\, and BAXTER ST (
 née Camera Club of New York).</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">He
  has had solo shows at Higher Pictures (which he joined in 2022)\, BAXTER 
 ST\, and Blue Sky Gallery. He has taught at the New School and Rutgers Uni
 versity and is a critic at Yale University. Currently\, Kha studies kung f
 u under Sifu Ken Lo.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">According to
  Kha\, he "takes after his great aunt\, who 'read too many books and wen
 t crazy'." </span></p><p class="p2"><span class="s2"><strong>Artist's we
 bsite:</strong><a href="https://tommykha.com">https://tommykha.com</a></sp
 an></p><p class="p2">  &#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  Yaël Ksander\n</div>\n<div>\n  Director
  of Communications and Marketing\n</div>\n<div>\n  Eskenazi School of Art\
 , Architecture + Design\n</div>\n<div>\n  <a href="mailto:yksander@iu.edu"
 >yksander@iu.edu</a>\n</div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2404999
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height
 /168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,768\,1152/32325_Tommy-Kha-photo-by-Jay_Amrahs
 -WEB.rev.1788361415.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Tommy Kha
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>The McKinney Visiting Artist Series presents a lect
 ure by Tommy Kha\, a photographer who explores the self-portraiture\, frag
 mentation\, and humor that are part of the Asian-American experience.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Eskenazi School|Fine Arts Building|lecture|McKinney Visit
 ing Artist|photography|Tommy Kha
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
