SUMMARY:Two Tales of Terror: J-Horror Unleashed with Best Wishes to All/ 
 Mina Ni Ko Are + Gozu | Friday Night Frights
DESCRIPTION:Snacks\, drinks in resealable/enclosed containers (there are 
 no cupholders in the Cinema!)\, and finger foods that do not emit a stron
 g odor or make a mess are allowed for this double feature. Alcohol\, ciga
 rettes\, electronic cigarettes\, and illicit drugs are prohibited at IU C
 inema.        Best Wishes to All/Mina ni ko are(Yûta Shimotsu\, Japan\, 
 2023): A young woman's visit to her grandparents' home leads to the disco
 very of what's brought them happiness\, a revelation that will lead her t
 o question her choices\, sanity\, and reality itself. [89 min\; horror\; 
 Japanese with English subtitles]        Gozu(Takashi Miike\, Japan\, 2003
 ): Acclaimed director Takashi Miike's unhinged Yakuza/horror film continu
 es to shock and amaze audiences decades after its original release. Minam
 i is sent to kill his mentor Ozaki (who is in the midst of a nervous brea
 kdown) but soon finds the simple hit quickly morphs into a terrifying and
  visceral journey into the unexplained and unknown. One of the films in M
 iike's oeuvre that continues to confound and haunt audiences\, which is s
 aying something! [129 min\; horror\; Japanese with English subtitles]
