 sidential appointment as a member of the National Council on the Arts\, a
 nd is the recipient of many of the most prestigious conducting awards. Sh
 e has conducted over 1\,600 orchestral works by more than 600 composers\,
 including over 135 works by women composers and over 150 premieres. After
  completing her bachelor's degree at Mannes\, Falletta earned master's an
 d doctoral degrees from The Juilliard School. When not on the podium\, sh
 e enjoys playing classical guitar\, writing\, cycling\, and yoga\, and is
  an avid reader.<br /><br /><strong>Brent Gault</strong> is professor of 
 music education at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. He has 
 taught elementary and early childhood music courses in Texas\, Wisconsin\
