CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Training, non-credit
  classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:High-stakes foreign policy and national security work require 
 more than classroom theory\, they require federal clearance.For students p
 ursuing diplomacy\, intelligence\, cyber policy\, or defense consulting\, 
 understanding how federal agencies evaluate suitability is essential.Join 
 the HLS Office of Policy Engagement and Strategic Partnerships for an excl
 usive\, off-the-record session with a federal Special Agent. Get direct pr
 actitioner insight into how federal agencies audit backgrounds\, evaluate 
 foreign connections\, and clear candidates for national security roles.Wha
 t We Are Covering in 60 Minutes:SF-86 &amp\; Global Footprints: How backgr
 ound investigators review study abroad trips\, foreign travel\, non-U.S. c
 itizen contacts\, and dual ties.Federal Standards vs. Real Life: The hard 
 lines on financial disclosures\, social media activity\, and federal drug 
 laws vs. state legalizations.    The Investigation Lifecycle: What actuall
 y happens during polygraphs\, field investigations\, and suitability revie
 ws.    Strategic Federal Timing: How to position yourself for agency spons
 orship early through federal programs and internships before graduation.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T181639Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2428156-unredacted-navigating-top-secr
 et-security
