  paintings in the galleries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and li
 ghting to communicate mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After findi
 ng inspiration in the galleries\, students will create their own still lif
 e paintings by arranging and observing objects at their table to tell thei
 r own unique stories!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educato
 r for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong><
 /p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of th
 e museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before explorin
 g the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'
 ll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own maste
 rpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. 
 <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older
 \, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
