SUMMARY:2026 Conference on Global Indigenous Studies (CGIS)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTSTAMP:20260121T152957Z
UID:20261113T050000Z-2180224@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20261113
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/137/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/592,63,1545,1015/31012_Corrected_CGIS_2026_Keynoters_2.rev.17
 76968582.jpg
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s
DESCRIPTION:CGIS 2026 is a transdisciplinary event that will bring togethe
 r national and international scholars\, educators\, practitioners\, studen
 ts\, policy makers\, activists\, academic institutions\, Indigenous organi
 zations\, grassroots organizations\, governmental and non-governmental org
 anizations. The participants in this conference will be involved in a loca
 l and global dialogue and exchange of ideas\, research\, and experiences o
 n the themes of the event.  Across the globe\, ethnic minorities and Indig
 enous communities have consistently strived to protect their rich cultural
  heritages and linguistic nuances from the influences of colonial powers\,
  expanding nation-states\, and the homogenizing impact of globalization. T
 his collective effort is increasingly recognized\, highlighted by the init
 iation of UNESCO's "Indigenous Languages Decade" (2022-2032) (https://www.
 unesco.org/en/decades/indigenous-languages/community/adhocgroups). The imp
 erative acknowledgment is that Indigenous languages\, along with the intri
 cate knowledge systems interwoven within them\, stand as crucial pillars f
 or preserving both biological and cultural pluralism.Proposal Submission (
 https://app.oxfordabstracts.com/auth?redirect=/stages/80009/submitter) Dea
 dline: April 30\, 2026Registration Costs (https://indianauniv.ungerboeck.c
 om/prod/emc00/register.aspx?aat=2f74415350355073564f6a6a762f41635557484844
 61566c746378794d6f4d4d67444739715679693634733d)  Early Bird Registration: 
 $60.00 (Before October 1\, 2026)  Standard Registration: $80.00 (October 1
  - November 15\, 2026)  &#160\;2026 Keynote Speakers:  Aluki Kotierk  Arma
 ndo Muyolema  Diego A. Titueña Matango  Teresa L. McCarty  &#160\;  Confe
 rence on Global and Indigenous Studies (CGIS) is made possible by the supp
 ort from:&#160\;African Studies Program (https://africanstudies.indiana.ed
 u/index.html?_gl=1*4pv3u5*_gcl_au*MTI2NDk4MTcxLjE3NzUwNTYwNjQ.*_ga*MTUxNzY
 zNjMwOS4xNzc1MDU2MDUw*_ga_61CH0D2DQW*czE3NzY5Njg4MDEkbzMzJGcwJHQxNzc2OTY4O
 DAxJGo2MCRsMCRoMA..)Arts and Humanities Futures – Indigenous Futures at 
 IUB (https://ahfutures.iu.edu/)Center for Latin American and Caribbean Stu
 dies (https://clacs.indiana.edu/index.html)Center for the Study of Global 
 Change (https://global.indiana.edu/index.html)Center for the Study of the 
 Middle East (https://csme.indiana.edu/index.html)East Asian Studies Center
  (https://easc.indiana.edu/index.html)Inner Asian and Uralic National Reso
 urce Center (https://iaunrc.indiana.edu/index.html)The Byrnes Institute (R
 EEI) (https://reei.indiana.edu/index.html)      &#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626T115941Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2170798-2026-conference-on-global-in
 digenous-studies-cgis
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>CGIS 2026</strong> is a transdisci
 plinary event that will bring together national and international scholars
 \, educators\, practitioners\, students\, policy makers\, activists\, acad
 emic institutions\, Indigenous organizations\, grassroots organizations\, 
 governmental and non-governmental organizations. The participants in this 
 conference will be involved in a local and global dialogue and exchange of
  ideas\, research\, and experiences on the themes of the event.</p><p>  Ac
 ross the globe\, ethnic minorities and Indigenous communities have consist
 ently strived to protect their rich cultural heritages and linguistic nuan
 ces from the influences of colonial powers\, expanding nation-states\, and
  the homogenizing impact of globalization. This collective effort is incre
 asingly recognized\, highlighted by the initiation of <a class="external" 
 href="https://www.unesco.org/en/decades/indigenous-languages/community/adh
 ocgroups">UNESCO's "Indigenous Languages Decade" (2022-2032)</a>. The impe
 rative acknowledgment is that Indigenous languages\, along with the intric
 ate knowledge systems interwoven within them\, stand as crucial pillars fo
 r preserving both biological and cultural pluralism.</p><p><em><strong><a 
 href="https://app.oxfordabstracts.com/auth?redirect=/stages/80009/submitte
 r">Proposal Submission</a> Deadline</strong></em>: April 30\, 2026</p><p><
 em><strong><a href="https://indianauniv.ungerboeck.com/prod/emc00/register
 .aspx?aat=2f74415350355073564f6a6a762f4163555748484461566c746378794d6f4d4d
 67444739715679693634733d">Registration Costs</a></strong></em><br />  Earl
 y Bird Registration: $60.00 (Before October 1\, 2026)<br />  Standard Regi
 stration: $80.00 (October 1 - November 15\, 2026)</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><s
 trong>2026 Keynote Speakers:</strong></p><p>  Aluki Kotierk</p><p>  Armand
 o Muyolema</p><p>  Diego A. Titueña Matango</p><p>  Teresa L. McCarty</p>
 <p><picture class="lw_image lw_image31013  lw_align_left"><source media="(
 max-width: 500px)" type="image/webp" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/im
 age/gid/137/width/500/height/420/31013_Update_of_Flyer_2-_2026_Conf._Globa
