 ttps://iuhealth.org/find-medical-services/positive-link-hiv-services" targ
 et="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-tabster="{&quot\;restorer&quot\
 ;:{&quot\;type&quot\;:1}}">Positive Link</a></span> provides <strong>free 
 and confidential HIV testing</strong> in Room 204 of the LGBTQ+ Culture Ce
 nter every Thursday from <strong>10:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m.</strong> during t
 he academic year. During the summer\, testing is available on the <strong>
 first and third Thursdays</strong> of each month.</p><p>  In addition\, du
 ring the academic year\, the <strong>Monroe County Health Department</stro
 ng> offers <strong>free chlamydia and gonorrhea testing</strong> on the <s
 trong>third Thursday of every month</strong>\, also from <strong>10:00 a.m
 . to 1:00 p.m.</strong> in Room 101.</p><p>  The LGBTQ+ Culture Center als
 o offers a variety of <strong>free safer sex supplies</strong>\, including
  condoms\, internal condoms\, dental dams\, lubricants\, and educational m
 aterials on proper use. These resources are available to all students\, fr
 ee of charge. You can find them in the kitchenette area near the back entr
 ance of the Center and are welcome to take what you need.</p><h3>  STI Tes
 ting &amp\; Safer Sex Resources Beyond Campus</h3><p>  Prioritizing your s
 exual health should be simple and accessible. In addition to services avai
 lable at the LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, students can receive testing on campu
 s through the <span class="___xxxjie0 f1w7gpdv f1gqqdtu" data-wra="1"><a c
 lass="fui-Link fai-bebop ___1v1lyro f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl f16muhyy f1k6
 fduh f1w7gpdv f1mo0ibp fjoy568 ff5ikls f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av 
 f13mvf36 f33ey8m f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 feiuef2 f1eh06m1 f54796x fhgqx1
 9 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f132whgj f1v74mp6 f1tsf1ni fnq52rx f16zlvvm" 
 tabindex="0" href="https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/medical/sti-testing/in
 dex.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-tabster="{&quot\;
 restorer&quot\;:{&quot\;type&quot\;:1}}">IU Student Health Center</a></spa
 n> or <a href="https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/health-answers/sexual-heal
 th/sti-testing-resources.html">visit several local organizations</a> that 
 offer free or low-cost testing and prevention services.</p><p>  Many of th
 ese providers offer confidential care\, safer sex supplies\, and supportiv
 e information about prevention\, treatment\, and sexual wellness. If you'r
 e unsure where to start\, we're happy to help connect you with resources t
 hat fit your needs.</p><p><strong>All Indiana University events\, groups\,
  activities\, educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome 
 all members of the Indiana University community.</strong></p>
