X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:The Texas Tenors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T010000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T010000
DTSTAMP:20260709T143914Z
UID:MEC-a16308a5a016c418f73c65af270d0d28@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T010000
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/2-scaled.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Happening,Live Music,Theatre &amp\; Entertainment
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260709
DESCRIPTION:Billboard #1 Recording Artists\, 3-time Emmy Award Winners & 
 2022 Texas Country Music Hall of Fame Inductees THE TEXAS TENORS are comin
 g to the Brown County Music Center!\nSince appearing on America’s Got Ta
 lent in 2009\, The Texas Tenors (JC Fisher\, Marcus Collins and John Hagen
 ) have released five studio albums\, three PBS Specials\, five DVDs\, mult
 iple singles and two children’s books that have earned them impressive r
 ecognition including three Emmy Awards\, The Gelett Burgess Award for Exce
 llence in Children’s Literature and the distinction of being Billboard M
 agazine’s #10 Classical Artist in the World. The Texas Tenors are the mo
 st successful music group and third highest selling artist in the history 
 of America’s Got Talent. \nThe group’s most recent albums “Outside 
 the Lines\,” “Rise\,” and “A Collection of Broadway and American C
 lassics” all debuted at No. 1 on the Billboard Charts. These classically
  trained\, versatile tenors have performed more than 2\,500 concerts aroun
 d the world including headline shows in Las Vegas\, China and a 24-city to
 ur of the United Kingdom. The show will feature music from their latest al
 bum along with rousing patriotic favorites and everything from country to 
 classical.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260709
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/the-texas-tenors/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
