BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2236877-micro-mythologies-world-mythology-made-miniature"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Micro-mythologies: World Mythology Made Miniature
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTSTAMP:20260312T103247Z
UID:20260926T040000Z-2236877@events.iu.edu__20261210
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1900,1900/30479_micromythologies_LW_avatar.rev.1773325700
 .png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:"Myths are the world's dreams."- Joseph Campbell.To believe is
  to be human.One of the greatest forces known to humankind\,belief is a un
 iversal impetus\, one that has raised and toppled temples\, instigated and
  eased wars\, and inspired written works\, both monumental and miniature. 
 This exhibition showcases a selection of minute materials that pertain to 
 mythologies and belief systems from across the world. From ancient Mesopot
 amian myth to modern Native American spirituality\, belief transcends time
  and history and intertwines human existence within our world.Micro-Mythol
 ogies: World Mythology Made Miniature is a miniature book exhibition which
  seeks to highlight some of our oldest and most powerful stories\, as well
  as those who preserved them.Mythological influence has shaped the world a
 round us. Whether that be through architecture\, art\, or literature\, myt
 hs serve as a testament to human cultural memory and the preservation of i
 ntangible tradition. Myths pull back the curtain of the past and reunite u
 s with the beliefs and stories of our ancestors.Most of these materials or
 iginate from the collection of prolific miniature book collector\, Ruth El
 izabeth Adomeit (1910-1996). Notable book artists highlighted inMicro-Myth
 ologies include Maryline Poole Adams\, Carol Cunningham\, Barbara J. Raheb
 \, Dianne Weiss\, and Gabrielle Fox.Micro-Mythologies: World Mythology Mad
 e Miniature is curated by Curatorial Assistant Jake Gentry\, with counsel 
 from Sarah McElroy Mitchell\, Curator of Religious Collections. In additio
 n\, exhibition design was done by Jenny Mack and graphic design by David O
 rr. This exhibition is on display in the Lilly Library Ball Room through D
 ecember 2026.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T194733Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2236877-micro-mythologies-world-
 mythology-made-miniature
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="auto">"</span><i><spa
 n data-contrast="auto">Myths are the world's dreams</span></i><span data-c
 ontrast="auto">."- Joseph Campbell.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;20
 1341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335551550&quot\;:2\,&quot\;335551620&quot\;:2\,&q
 uot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><
 p><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\
 ;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><strong><i><span d
 ata-contrast="auto">To believe is to be human</span></i></strong><span dat
 a-contrast="auto">.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0
 \,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span><
 /p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;2013
 41983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:
 288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">One of the greatest forces 
 known to humankind\,</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">belief </span></i
 ><span data-contrast="auto">is a universal impetus\, one that has raised a
 nd toppled temples\, instigated and eased wars\, and inspired written work
 s\, both monumental and miniature. This exhibition showcases a selection o
 f minute materials that pertain to mythologies and belief systems from acr
 oss the world. From ancient Mesopotamian myth to modern Native American sp
 irituality\, belief transcends time and history and intertwines human exis
 tence within our world.</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Micro-Mytholog
 ies: World Mythology Made Miniature </span></i><span data-contrast="auto">
 is a miniature book exhibition which seeks to highlight some of our oldest
  and most powerful stories\, as well as those who preserved them.</span><s
 pan data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16
 777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="a
 uto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;33555
 7856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span da
 ta-contrast="auto">Mythological influence has shaped the world around us. 
 Whether that be through architecture\, art\, or literature\, myths serve a
 s a testament to human cultural memory and the preservation of intangible 
 tradition. Myths pull back the curtain of the past and reunite us with the
  beliefs and stories of our ancestors.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\
 ;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&qu
 ot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp-
 props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot
 \;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Most of 
 these materials originate from the collection of prolific miniature book c
 ollector\, Ruth Elizabeth Adomeit (1910-1996). Notable book artists highli
 ghted in</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Micro-Mythologies </span></i>
 <span data-contrast="auto">include Maryline Poole Adams\, Carol Cunningham
 \, Barbara J. Raheb\, Dianne Weiss\, and Gabrielle Fox.</span><span data-c
 cp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&q
 uot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></spa
 n><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\
 ;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><i><span data-cont
 rast="auto">Micro-Mythologies: World Mythology Made Miniature </span></i><
 span data-contrast="auto">is curated by Curatorial Assistant Jake Gentry\,
  with counsel from Sarah McElroy Mitchell\, Curator of Religious Collectio
 ns. In addition\, exhibition design was done by Jenny Mack and graphic des
 ign by David Orr. This exhibition is on display in the Lilly Library Ball 
 Room through December 2026.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&
 quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}">
 </span></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
